1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
[Captioning sponsored by
A&E TELEVISION NETWORKS]

2
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
( grunts angrily )

3
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Lizzy:
YOU ARE THE LAST MAN
IN THE WORLD

4
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,000
WHOM I COULD EVER MARRY.

5
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
DO YOU THINK THAT ANY
CONSIDERATION WOULD TEMPT ME?

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
YOUR ARROGANCE, YOUR CONCEIT

7
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
AND YOUR SELFISH DISDAIN
FOR THE FEELINGS OF OTHERS.

8
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
MY OPINION OF YOU WAS DECIDED

9
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
WHEN I HEARD
MR. WICKHAM'S STORY

10
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
OF YOUR DEALINGS WITH HIM.

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
WELL, AT LEAST IN THAT,
I MAY DEFEND MYSELF.

12
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Darcy:
COULD YOU EXPECT ME TO REJOICE

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
IN THE INFERIORITY
OF YOUR CONNECTIONS?

14
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
TO CONGRATULATE MYSELF
ON THE HOPE OF RELATIONS

15
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
WHOSE CONDITION IN LIFE
IS SO DECIDEDLY BELOW MY OWN?

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Lizzy:
YOU ARE MISTAKEN, MR. DARCY.

17
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
THE MODE OF YOUR DECLARATION
MERELY SPARED ME THE CONCERN

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,000
I MIGHT HAVE FELT
IN REFUSING YOU

19
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
HAD YOU BEHAVED
IN A MORE GENTLEMANLIKE MANNER.

20
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Lady Catherine:
WHO'S THERE,
FITZWILLIAM?

21
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
DARCY, WE'D QUITE
DESPAIRED OF YOU!

22
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Lady Catherine:
IS THAT MY NEPHEW?
WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN?

23
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
LET HIM COME IN
AND EXPLAIN HIMSELF.

24
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
NO.

25
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
YOU WILL FORGIVE ME.

26
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
YOU WILL FORGIVE ME.

27
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
DARCY, YOU ARE UNWELL?

28
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
I AM VERY WELL, THANK YOU

29
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
BUT I HAVE PRESSING BUSINESS.

30
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
YOU WILL FORGIVE ME.

31
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
MAKE MY APOLOGIES
TO LADY CATHERINE.

32
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
( door closes )

33
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,000
TO MISS ELIZABETH BENNET.

34
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
BE NOT ALARMED, MADAM,
ON RECEIVING THIS LETTER

35
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
THAT IT CONTAIN ANY REPETITION
OF THOSE SENTIMENTS

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
OR RENEWAL OF THOSE OFFERS

37
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
WHICH WERE, THIS EVENING,
SO DISGUSTING TO YOU.

38
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
BUT I MUST BE ALLOWED
TO DEFEND MYSELF

39
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
AGAINST THE CHARGES
LAID AT MY DOOR

40
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
IN PARTICULAR THOSE
RELATING TO MR. WICKHAM

41
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
WHICH, IF TRUE,
WOULD INDEED BE GRIEVOUS

42
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
BUT ARE WHOLLY
WITHOUT FOUNDATION

43
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,000
AND WHICH I CAN ONLY REFUTE

44
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
BY LAYING BEFORE YOU
HIS CONNECTION WITH MY FAMILY.

45
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
MR. WICKHAM IS THE SON
OF A VERY RESPECTABLE MAN

46
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
WHO HAD THE MANAGEMENT
OF OUR FAMILY ESTATES

47
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
AND MY OWN FATHER
WAS FOND OF HIM

48
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
AND HELD HIM IN HIGH ESTEEM.

49
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:45,000
WE PLAYED TOGETHER AS BOYS.

50
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
AFTER HIS FATHER'S EARLY DEATH

51
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
MY FATHER SUPPORTED HIM
AT SCHOOL

52
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
AND AFTERWARDS AT CAMBRIDGE

53
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
AND HOPED HE WOULD MAKE
THE CHURCH HIS PROFESSION.

54
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
BUT BY THEN,
GEORGE WICKHAM'S HABITS

55
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:03,000
WERE AS DISSOLUTE
AS HIS MANNERS WERE ENGAGING.

56
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:13,000
MY OWN EXCELLENT FATHER
DIED FIVE YEARS AGO

57
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
AND HIS ATTACHMENT
TO MR. WICKHAM

58
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
WAS TO THE LAST SO STEADY

59
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
THAT HE DESIRED THAT A VALUABLE
FAMILY LIVING MIGHT BE HIS

60
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
AS SOON AS IT WAS VACANT.

61
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
MR. WICKHAM DECLINED INTEREST
IN THE CHURCH AS A CAREER

62
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
BUT REQUESTED, AND WAS GRANTED

63
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:31,000
THE SUM OF £3,000
INSTEAD OF THE LIVING.

64
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:35,000
HE EXPRESSED AN INTENTION
OF STUDYING THE LAW.

65
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:40,000
I WISHED RATHER THAN
BELIEVED HIM TO BE SINCERE.

66
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
THANK YOU.

67
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
I'M MOST EXCEEDINGLY OBLIGED.

68
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:54,000
ALL CONNECTION BETWEEN US
SEEMED NOW DISSOLVED.

69
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,000
GEORGIANA.

70
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:05,000
BEING NOW
FREE FROM ALL RESTRAINT

71
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:09,000
HIS LIFE WAS ONE
OF IDLENESS AND DISSIPATION.

72
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
HOW HE LIVED, I KNOW NOT.

73
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
BUT LAST SUMMER,
OUR PATHS CROSSED AGAIN

74
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
UNDER THE MOST PAINFUL
CIRCUMSTANCES

75
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
WHICH I MYSELF
WOULD WISH TO FORGET.

76
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:25,000
MY SISTER GEORGIANA, WHO IS
MORE THAN TEN YEARS MY JUNIOR

77
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:30,000
WAS LEFT TO THE GUARDIANSHIP OF
COLONEL FITZWILLIAM AND MYSELF.

78
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
ABOUT A YEAR AGO, SHE WAS TAKEN
FROM SCHOOL TO RAMSGATE

79
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
AND PLACED
IN THE CARE OF A MRS. YOUNGE

80
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
IN WHOSE CHARACTER WE WERE
MOST UNHAPPILY DECEIVED.

81
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
AND THITHER
ALSO WENT MR. WICKHAM

82
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:47,000
UNDOUBTEDLY BY DESIGN.

83
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
SHE WAS PERSUADED
TO BELIEVE HERSELF IN LOVE

84
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
AND TO CONSENT TO AN ELOPEMENT.

85
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:58,000
SHE WAS THEN BUT 15 YEARS OLD.

86
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
A DAY OR TWO
BEFORE THE INTENDED ELOPEMENT

87
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:06,000
I JOINED THEM UNEXPECTEDLY.

88
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
UNABLE TO SUPPORT THE IDEA
OF GRIEVING A BROTHER

89
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
WHOM SHE LOOKED UP TO
ALMOST AS A FATHER

90
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
SHE ACKNOWLEDGED
THE WHOLE PLAN TO ME AT ONCE.

91
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
YOU MAY IMAGINE
WHAT I FELT AND HOW I ACTED.

92
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:34,000
MR. WICKHAM
LEFT THE PLACE IMMEDIATELY.

93
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:42,000
COME.

94
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
MR. WICKHAM
RELINQUISHED HIS OBJECT

95
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:50,000
WHICH WAS OF COURSE
MY SISTER'S FORTUNE OF £30,000.

96
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:54,000
A SECONDARY MOTIVE MUST HAVE
BEEN TO REVENGE HIMSELF ON ME.

97
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:58,000
HAD HE SUCCEEDED, HIS REVENGE
WOULD HAVE BEEN COMPLETE.

98
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
THIS, MADAM,
IS A FAITHFUL NARRATIVE

99
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:06,000
OF ALL MY DEALINGS
WITH MR. WICKHAM.

100
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:51,000
( mumbling
with mouth full )

101
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
OH, YOU DO
LOOK PALE, LIZZY.

102
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
WHY DON'T YOU
HAVE SOME BREAKFAST?

103
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
I'M SURE IT WILL DO YOU GOOD.

104
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
OH, NO, I'M WELL, CHARLOTTE.

105
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
I THINK I'VE
STAYED INDOORS TOO LONG.

106
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
FRESH AIR IS
ALL I NEED.

107
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
THE WOODS AROUND ROSINGS
ARE BEAUTIFUL

108
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:11,000
AT THIS TIME OF YEAR.

109
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
MISS BENNET.

110
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
MR. DARCY.

111
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:59,000
I'VE BEEN WALKING
THE GROVE SOME TIME

112
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
IN THE HOPE OF MEETING YOU.

113
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:05,000
WILL YOU DO ME THE HONOR
OF READING THIS LETTER?

114
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Darcy:
THIS, MADAM,
IS A FAITHFUL NARRATIVE

115
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
OF ALL MY DEALINGS
WITH MR. WICKHAM

116
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
AND FOR ITS TRUTH I CAN APPEAL

117
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
TO THE TESTIMONY
OF COLONEL FITZWILLIAM

118
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
WHO KNOWS EVERY PARTICULAR
OF THESE TRANSACTIONS.

119
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,000
I KNOW NOT
UNDER WHAT FALSEHOOD

120
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
MR. WICKHAM
IMPOSED HIMSELF ON YOU

121
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
BUT I HOPE YOU WILL ACQUIT ME
OF CRUELTY TOWARDS HIM.

122
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Wickham:
I FOUND AS THE TIME DREW NEAR

123
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
THAT I HAD BETTER NOT
MEET MR. DARCY.

124
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
SCENES MIGHT ARISE
UNPLEASANT TO MORE THAN MYSELF.

125
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
THE OTHER CHARGE
LEVELED AT ME IS THAT

126
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
REGARDLESS OF THE SENTIMENTS
OF EITHER PARTY

127
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
I DETACHED MR. BINGLEY
FROM YOUR SISTER.

128
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
I HAVE NO WISH TO DENY THIS

129
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:57,000
NOR CAN I BLAME MYSELF FOR ANY
OF MY ACTIONS IN THIS MATTER.

130
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
OH!

131
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
I HAD NOT LONG BEEN
IN HERTFORDSHIRE

132
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
BEFORE I SAW THAT
BINGLEY ADMIRED YOUR SISTER

133
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
BUT IT WAS NOT
UNTIL THE DANCE AT NETHERFIELD

134
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
THAT I SUSPECTED
A SERIOUS ATTACHMENT.

135
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
HIS PARTIALITY WAS CLEAR

136
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,000
BUT THOUGH SHE RECEIVED
HIS ATTENTIONS WITH PLEASURE

137
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:18,000
I DID NOT DETECT ANY
SYMPTOMS OF PECULIAR REGARD.

138
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
THE SERENITY OF HER
COUNTENANCE CONVINCED ME

139
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
THAT HER HEART WAS NOT
TO BE EASILY TOUCHED.

140
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
INSUFFERABLE PRESUMPTION!

141
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
I DID NOT BELIEVE THIS
BECAUSE I WISHED IT.

142
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
I BELIEVED IT
ON IMPARTIAL CONVICTION.

143
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,000
OH, VERY IMPARTIAL!

144
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
YOU MISSED
THE TWO GENTLEMEN.

145
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
THEY CAME TO TAKE THEIR LEAVE!

146
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,000
MR. DARCY CAME HERE?

147
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
YES, BUT HE WENT
AWAY AGAIN DIRECTLY.

148
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
BUT THE COLONEL WAITED FOR YOU
OVER HALF AN HOUR!

149
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
NOW THEY ARE BOTH GONE
OUT OF THE COUNTRY!

150
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:49,000
I DARESAY WE SHALL BE ABLE
TO BEAR THE DEPRIVATION.

151
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:01,000
AS TO MY OBJECTIONS
TO THE MARRIAGE

152
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
THE SITUATION OF YOUR FAMILY,
THOUGH OBJECTIONABLE

153
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:08,000
WAS NOTHING IN COMPARISON WITH
THE TOTAL WANT OF PROPRIETY

154
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
SO FREQUENTLY
BETRAYED BY YOUR MOTHER

155
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:14,000
YOUR YOUNGER SISTERS, AND
EVEN OCCASIONALLY YOUR FATHER.

156
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
( Mary playing piano
and singing badly )

157
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,000
THAT WILL DO
EXTREMELY WELL, CHILD.

158
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
YOU HAVE DELIGHTED US
LONG ENOUGH.

159
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
NOW, THERE WILL BE
A GREAT MARRIAGE!

160
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,000
AND YOU KNOW
THAT WILL THROW THE GIRLS

161
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:34,000
INTO THE PATH OF OTHER RICH MEN.

162
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,000
MY FRIEND LEFT FOR LONDON
THE FOLLOWING DAY.

163
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
THERE I POINTED OUT TO HIM
THE CERTAIN EVILS

164
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
OF HIS CHOICE OF YOUR SISTER
AS A PROSPECTIVE BRIDE.

165
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
IT WAS NOT DIFFICULT
TO CONVINCE HIM

166
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
OF YOUR SISTER'S
INDIFFERENCE TO HIM.

167
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:56,000
I CANNOT BLAME MYSELF
FOR HAVING DONE THUS MUCH.

168
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
FOR DESTROYING ALL HER HOPE
OF HAPPINESS?

169
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
YES, I AM SURE YOU DO NOT
BLAME YOURSELF, HATEFUL MAN.

170
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
THERE IS ONE PART
OF MY CONDUCT IN THE AFFAIR

171
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
ON WHICH I DO NOT REFLECT
WITH SATISFACTION.

172
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
OH, REALLY? ASTONISH ME.

173
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
THAT IS,
THAT I CONCEALED FROM HIM

174
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:16,000
YOUR SISTER'S BEING IN TOWN.

175
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
PERHAPS THIS CONCEALMENT
WAS BENEATH ME.

176
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
IT IS DONE, HOWEVER,
AND IT WAS DONE FOR THE BEST.

177
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
ON THIS SUBJECT,
I HAVE NOTHING MORE TO SAY

178
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
AND NO OTHER APOLOGY TO OFFER.

179
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
INSUFFERABLE!

180
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Charlotte:
LIZZY!

181
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Collins:
CHARLOTTE, MY DEAR,
WE WILL BE LATE.

182
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,000
LIZZY!

183
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Collins:
I HAVE BEEN ATTEMPTING TO
RECOLLECT THE NUMBER OF TIMES

184
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
LADY CATHERINE DE BOURGH
HAS INVITED US

185
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
SINCE YOUR ARRIVAL HERE.

186
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
I BELIEVE IT MAY BE
AS MANY AS TEN INVITATIONS.

187
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Maria:
11, COUNTING THIS ONE.

188
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
ELEVEN, THERE.

189
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:52,000
YOU HAVE INDEED
BEEN FAVORED WITH
PECULIAR CONDESCENSION.

190
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
DO YOU NOT AGREE,
MISS ELIZABETH?

191
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
OH, YES.

192
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,000
INDEED. HOW COULD
ANYBODY THINK OTHERWISE?

193
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
AND THIS IS TO BE
YOUR LAST INVITATION...

194
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
ON THIS VISIT, AT LEAST.

195
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
YES, IT IS TRULY
A VERY CRUEL DEPRIVATION.

196
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
INDEED, I HARDLY KNOW
HOW I SHALL BEAR

197
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
THE LOSS OF LADY
CATHERINE'S COMPANY.

198
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
YOU FEEL IT KEENLY.

199
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:15,000
YES, OF COURSE YOU DO,
MY POOR YOUNG COUSIN.

200
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:19,000
Lady Catherine:
THEY WERE SUCH FINE YOUNG MEN

201
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
AND SO PARTICULARLY
ATTACHED TO ME.

202
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
THEY WERE EXCESSIVELY
SORRY TO GO

203
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
BUT SO THEY ALWAYS ARE.

204
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
THE DEAR COLONEL RALLIED
HIS SPIRITS TOLERABLY

205
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:35,000
BUT DARCY SEEMED TO
FEEL IT MOST ACUTELY.

206
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,000
HIS ATTACHMENT TO ROSINGS

207
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:42,000
CERTAINLY
INCREASES.

208
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,000
YOU ARE VERY DULL THIS EVENING,
MISS ELIZABETH BENNET.

209
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
YOU HAVE SCARCE
SPOKE TWO WORDS TOGETHER.

210
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
ARE YOU SO OUT OF SPIRITS?

211
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
NO, INDEED, MADAM.

212
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
BUT OF COURSE YOU ARE...

213
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
TO BE GOING AWAY
YOURSELF.

214
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
WHO INDEED WOULD NOT BE SAD
TO BE DEPRIVED OF ROSINGS

215
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
AND INDEED
OF THE GRACIOUS CONDESCEN...

216
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,000
YOU WILL WRITE
TO YOUR MOTHER

217
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
AND TELL HER YOU WISH
TO STAY A LITTLE LONGER.

218
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:08,000
SHE COULD CERTAINLY SPARE YOU
FOR ANOTHER FORTNIGHT.

219
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
BUT MY FATHER CANNOT.

220
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
HE WROTE LAST WEEK
TO HURRY MY RETURN.

221
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
YOUR LADYSHIP
IS VERY KIND

222
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
BUT I BELIEVE
WE MUST LEAVE

223
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,000
AS PLANNED,
ON FRIDAY.

224
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
YOUR FATHER MAY SPARE
YOU IF YOUR MOTHER CAN.

225
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,000
DAUGHTERS ARE NEVER
OF MUCH CONSEQUENCE TO A FATHER

226
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
AND IF YOU WILL STAY
ANOTHER MONTH COMPLETE

227
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:31,000
IT WILL BE IN MY POWER TO
TAKE YOU AS FAR AS LONDON MYSELF

228
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
IN THE BAROUCHE BOX.

229
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
FOR I CANNOT
BEAR THE IDEA

230
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
OF TWO YOUNG WOMEN

231
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,000
TRAVELING POST
BY THEMSELVES.

232
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
IT IS HIGHLY IMPROPER.

233
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:46,000
I AM EXCESSIVELY ATTENTIVE
TO ALL THOSE THINGS.

234
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,000
MY UNCLE IS
TO SEND A SERVANT

235
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
WHEN WE CHANGE TO THE POST.

236
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:53,000
OH... YOUR UNCLE.

237
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
HE KEEPS A MANSERVANT, DOES HE?

238
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,000
I'M VERY GLAD YOU HAVE SOMEBODY

239
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
WHO THINKS
OF THESE THINGS.

240
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,000
WHERE WILL YOU
CHANGE HORSES?

241
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,000
OH, BROMLEY, OF COURSE.

242
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:07,000
MENTION MY NAME AT THE BELL
AND THEY WILL ATTEND YOU.

243
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
YOUR LADYSHIP IS VERY KIND.

244
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
INDEED, WE ARE ALL
INFINITELY INDEBTED

245
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
TO YOUR LADYSHIP'S
KINDLY BESTOWED SOLICITUDE...

246
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:18,000
YES, YES, BUT THIS IS
ALL EXTREMELY VEXING.

247
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,000
I'M QUITE PUT OUT!

248
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
WHY, MARIA,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

249
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
I THOUGHT THE TRUNKS WENT
OUTSIDE BEFORE BREAKFAST.

250
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
BUT LADY CATHERINE WAS
SO SEVERE LAST EVENING

251
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
ABOUT THE ONLY RIGHT WAY
TO PLACE GOWNS

252
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,000
THAT I COULDN'T SLEEP

253
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,000
AND I AM DETERMINED
TO START AFRESH.

254
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
MARIA, THIS
IS YOUR TRUNK;

255
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
THESE ARE YOUR GOWNS.

256
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
YOU MAY ARRANGE THEM
IN ANY WAY YOU WISH.

257
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,000
( whispering ):
LADY CATHERINE
WILL NEVER KNOW.

258
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Collins:
MY DEAR SISTER,
YOU WILL HAVE MUCH

259
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,000
TO TELL YOUR FATHER.

260
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Charlotte:
BRING THAT ONE AROUND HERE.

261
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Maria:
SCARCELY A DAY HAS PASSED
WITHOUT SOME NEW KINDNESS.

262
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:56,000
DO MAKE SURE
THEY'RE SECURE.

263
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,000
WELL, COUSIN

264
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
YOU HAVE SEEN
FOR YOURSELF NOW

265
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
THE HAPPINESS
OF OUR SITUATION.

266
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
OUR INTIMACY
AT ROSINGS IS A BLESSING

267
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
OF WHICH
FEW COULD BOAST.

268
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
INDEED, THEY COULD NOT.

269
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
INDEED.

270
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,000
AND NOW YOU HAVE
WITNESSED OUR FELICITY

271
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
PERHAPS YOU MAY THINK
THAT YOUR FRIEND

272
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
HAS MADE A VERY
FORTUNATE ALLIANCE.

273
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
PERHAPS MORE SO THAN...

274
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:23,000
BUT ON THIS POINT, IT WILL
BE AS WELL TO BE SILENT.

275
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
YOU ARE VERY GOOD.

276
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
ONLY LET ME
ASSURE YOU THAT I CAN

277
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
FROM MY HEART

278
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:35,000
MOST CORDIALLY WISH YOU
EQUAL FELICITY IN MARRIAGE.

279
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
CHARLOTTE AND I

280
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,000
HAVE BUT ONE MIND
AND ONE WAY OF THINKING.

281
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:44,000
WE SEEM TO HAVE BEEN
DESIGNED FOR EACH OTHER.

282
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
OH, LIZZY, IT SEEMS
BUT A DAY OR TWO

283
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
SINCE WE FIRST CAME

284
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
AND YET HOW MANY THINGS
HAVE HAPPENED.

285
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
A GREAT MANY INDEED.

286
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
WE HAVE DINED NINE TIMES
AT ROSINGS.

287
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:19,000
OH, HOW MUCH
I SHALL HAVE TO TELL.

288
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:24,000
HOW MUCH I SHALL
HAVE TO CONCEAL.

289
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,000
YOU MUST ALLOW ME TO TELL YOU

290
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:38,000
HOW ARDENTLY
I ADMIRE AND LOVE YOU.

291
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
LIZZY!

292
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:05,000
LIZZY!

293
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Lydia:
TO SEE YOUR FACES
WHEN YOU LOOKED UP.

294
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
I'LL WAGER
YOU DIDN'T EXPECT

295
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
WE'D COME
TO MEET YOU.

296
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
NO, WE DID NOT.

297
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,000
THERE.

298
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
IS NOT THIS NICE?

299
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,000
COLD HAM AND PORK AND SALADS
AND EVERY GOOD THING.

300
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,000
AND WE MEAN
TO TREAT YOU ALL.

301
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
BUT YOU MUST LEND US
THE MONEY.

302
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
WE SPENT ALL OURS, LOOK.

303
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
I DON'T THINK
IT'S VERY PRETTY

304
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
BUT I THOUGHT I MIGHT
AS WELL BUY IT.

305
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,000
IT'S VILE,
ISN'T IT?

306
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
WHAT POSSESSED YOU
TO BUY IT, LYDIA?

307
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
THERE WERE OTHERS
MUCH UGLIER IN THE SHOP.

308
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
I SHALL PULL IT TO PIECES
AS SOON AS WE GET HOME

309
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,000
AND SEE IF I CAN
MAKE IT UP ANY BETTER.

310
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,000
IT DOESN'T SIGNIFY
WHAT ANYONE WEARS

311
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
FOR THE REGIMENT WILL LEAVE
AND BE AT BRIGHTON

312
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,000
FOR THE WHOLE SUMMER.

313
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
OUR HEARTS ARE BROKEN.

314
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:51,000
WE WANT PAPA TO TAKE US
TO BRIGHTON, BUT HE WILL NOT.

315
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,000
I'M GLAD TO HEAR IT.

316
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,000
OH, BUT
SHOULDN'T YOU LIKE

317
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,000
TO GO
TO BRIGHTON, LIZZY?

318
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
INDEED,
I SHOULD NOT.

319
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
SHE WOULD LOVE IT
ABOVE ALL THINGS

320
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
WHEN SHE HEARS THE NEWS

321
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
ABOUT A CERTAIN PERSON
WE ALL KNOW.

322
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,000
SHALL WE TELL HER?

323
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
YES, AND WATCH
TO SEE IF SHE BLUSHES.

324
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
YOU MAY GO NOW.

325
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
WE'LL CALL YOU
IF YOU'RE NEEDED AGAIN.

326
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:13,000
VERY GOOD, MA'AM.

327
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:18,000
WICKHAM IS NOT TO MARRY
MARY KING AFTER ALL.

328
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
SHE'S BEEN TAKEN AWAY
BY HER UNCLE TO LIVERPOOL

329
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
AND WICKHAM IS SAFE.

330
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,000
PERHAPS WE SHOULD SAY
MARY KING IS SAFE.

331
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,000
BUT WAS THERE A VERY STRONG
ATTRACTION BETWEEN THEM?

332
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,000
NOT ON HIS SIDE, I'M SURE.

333
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,000
I SHOULDN'T THINK
HE CARED THREE STRAWS
ABOUT HER.

334
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
WHO COULD ABOUT
SUCH A NASTY,
FRECKLED LITTLE THING?

335
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
DON'T LOOK AT ME
LIKE THAT, LIZZY.

336
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
I KNOW YOU THINK
AS ILL OF HER
AS I DO.

337
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,000
PASS THE CELERY.

338
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
AREN'T YOU GLAD WE CAME?

339
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,000
WE SHALL BE A MERRY PARTY
ON THE JOURNEY HOME.

340
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Lydia:
KITTY, YOU'RE
SQUASHING MY BANDBOX!

341
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Kitty:
YOU SHOULD HAVE PUT IT
ON THE ROOF-- THERE ISN'T ROOM.

342
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Lydia:
IF YOU DIDN'T LOLLOP ABOUT,
THERE'D BE ROOM FOR US ALL

343
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,000
AND THE BANDBOX.

344
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Kitty:
I DO NOT LOLLOP!

345
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
MR. DARCY PROPOSED?

346
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:03,000
I CAN SCARCE BELIEVE IT.

347
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,000
NOT THAT ANYONE'S ADMIRING YOU
SHOULD BE ASTONISHING.

348
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
BUT HE ALWAYS
SEEMS SO SEVERE.

349
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
SO COLD, APPARENTLY.

350
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
AND YET HE WAS IN LOVE
WITH YOU ALL THE TIME.

351
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
POOR MR. DARCY.

352
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
I CONFESS I CANNOT FEEL
SO MUCH COMPASSION FOR HIM.

353
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,000
HE HAS OTHER FEELINGS

354
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:22,000
WHICH WILL SOON DRIVE AWAY
ANY REGARD HE FELT FOR ME.

355
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,000
YOU DO NOT BLAME ME
FOR REFUSING HIM?

356
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
BLAME YOU?

357
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
OH, NO.

358
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
BUT YOU DO BLAME ME

359
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,000
FOR SPEAKING
SO WARMLY OF WICKHAM?

360
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
NO, HOW COULD YOU HAVE KNOWN
ABOUT HIS VICIOUS CHARACTER?

361
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
IF INDEED HE WAS SO VERY BAD.

362
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
BUT I CANNOT BELIEVE

363
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,000
MR. DARCY WOULD FABRICATE
SUCH A DREADFUL SLANDER

364
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
INVOLVING HIS OWN SISTER, TOO.

365
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
NO, IT MUST BE TRUE.

366
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:52,000
PERHAPS THERE HAS BEEN
SOME TERRIBLE MISTAKE.

367
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
NO, JANE, THAT WON'T DO.

368
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
YOU'LL NEVER BE ABLE
TO MAKE THEM BOTH GOOD.

369
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
THERE IS JUST ENOUGH
MERIT BETWEEN THEM

370
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
TO MAKE ONE GOOD SORT OF MAN.

371
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
AND FOR MY PART

372
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
I'M INCLINED TO BELIEVE
IT'S ALL MR. DARCY'S.

373
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
POOR MR. DARCY.

374
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
POOR MR. WICKHAM.

375
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,000
THERE IS SUCH AN EXPRESSION
OF GOODNESS IN HIS COUNTENANCE.

376
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:16,000
YES, I'M AFRAID ONE
HAS ALL THE GOODNESS

377
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:20,000
AND THE OTHER
ALL THE APPEARANCE OF IT.

378
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,000
BUT, LIZZY

379
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
I'M SURE WHEN YOU
FIRST READ THAT LETTER

380
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
YOU COULD NOT HAVE
MADE SO LIGHT OF IT

381
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
AS YOU DO NOW.

382
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
INDEED I COULD NOT.

383
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
I WAS VERY
UNCOMFORTABLE.

384
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:35,000
TILL THAT MOMENT,
I NEVER KNEW MYSELF.

385
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
AND I HAD NO JANE TO COMFORT ME.

386
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:44,000
OH, HOW I WANTED YOU.

387
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
THERE IS ONE POINT ON
WHICH I WANT YOUR ADVICE.

388
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:52,000
SHOULD OUR GENERAL ACQUAINTANCE
BE INFORMED

389
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:56,000
OF WICKHAM'S TRUE CHARACTER?

390
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:59,000
SURELY THERE CAN BE NO OCCASION
TO EXPOSE HIM SO CRUELLY.

391
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
WHAT IS YOUR OWN OPINION?

392
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:04,000
THAT IT OUGHT
NOT TO BE ATTEMPTED.

393
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:07,000
MR. DARCY HAS NOT AUTHORIZED ME
TO MAKE IT PUBLIC

394
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:11,000
ESPECIALLY
AS REGARDS HIS SISTER.

395
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,000
AND FOR THE REST,
WHO WOULD BELIEVE IT?

396
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:16,000
THE GENERAL PREJUDICE
AGAINST MR. DARCY IS SO VIOLENT

397
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,000
AND WICKHAM WILL SOON BE GONE.

398
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:21,000
I BELIEVE WE SHOULD SAY NOTHING
ABOUT IT AT PRESENT.

399
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:25,000
YES, I AGREE.

400
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,000
PERHAPS HE IS SORRY NOW
FOR WHAT HE HAS DONE

401
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,000
AND IS ANXIOUS
TO REESTABLISH HIS
CHARACTER IN THE WORLD.

402
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,000
WE MUST NOT
MAKE HIM DESPERATE.

403
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:37,000
OH, JANE, I WISH I COULD THINK
SO WELL OF PEOPLE AS YOU DO.

404
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:42,000
Lydia:
WON'T YOU SPEAK TO PAPA, LIZZY,
ABOUT OUR GOING TO BRIGHTON?

405
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,000
YOU KNOW HE LISTENS
TO YOUR ADVICE.

406
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:46,000
YOU FLATTER ME, LYDIA,
BUT IN ANY CASE

407
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:49,000
I SHOULDN'T ATTEMPT
TO PERSUADE HIM.

408
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,000
I THINK IT'S
A VERY GOOD THING

409
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:53,000
THAT THE REGIMENT SHOULD
BE REMOVED FROM MERYTON

410
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:56,000
AND THAT WE SHOULD BE REMOVED
FROM THE REGIMENT.

411
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
OH, LIZZY, HOW CAN
YOU SAY SUCH A THING?!

412
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
VERY EASILY, MUM.

413
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,000
IF ONE POOR COMPANY OF MILITIA

414
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,000
CAN CAUSE SUCH HAVOC
IN OUR FAMILY

415
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
WHAT WOULD A WHOLE CAMP
FULL OF SOLDIERS DO?

416
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:09,000
A WHOLE CAMP FULL OF SOLDIERS.

417
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Mrs. Bennet:
I REMEMBER WHEN
I WAS A GIRL.

418
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,000
I CRIED FOR TWO DAYS TOGETHER

419
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:15,000
WHEN COLONEL MILLER'S REGIMENT
WENT AWAY.

420
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,000
I THOUGHT I SHOULD
HAVE BROKE MY HEART.

421
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
WELL, I'M SURE
I SHALL BREAK MINE.

422
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,000
AND I.

423
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
THERE, THERE, MY DEARS.

424
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:26,000
BUT YOUR FATHER IS DETERMINED
TO BE CRUEL.

425
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
I CONFESS I AM.

426
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:30,000
I'M SORRY TO BE BREAKING
SO MANY HEARTS

427
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
BUT I'VE NOT THE SMALLEST
INTENTION OF YIELDING.

428
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,000
I SHALL NOT BREAK
MY HEART, PAPA.

429
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,000
THE PLEASURES
OF BRIGHTON

430
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,000
WOULD HAVE NO
CHARMS FOR ME.

431
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
I SHOULD PREFER A BOOK.

432
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:40,000
OHH!

433
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:43,000
MRS. FORSTER SAYS SHE PLANS
TO GO SEA-BATHING.

434
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:47,000
I'M SURE I SHOULD LOVE
TO GO SEA-BATHING.

435
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:50,000
A LITTLE SEA-BATHING
WOULD SET ME UP FOREVER.

436
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:51,000
AND YET I AM UNMOVED.

437
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:55,000
WELL, WELL, I'M GLAD
YOU'RE COME BACK, LIZZY.

438
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:57,000
I'M GLAD YOU'RE
COME BACK, JANE.

439
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:59,000
( door opens and closes )

440
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:02,000
( whimpering )

441
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:07,000
I WANT TO GO TO BRIGHTON!

442
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,000
YOU ARE NOT HAPPY, JANE.

443
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:33,000
IT PAINS ME
TO SEE IT.

444
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,000
IT IS JUST THAT I DID...

445
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:37,000
I'M AFRAID I STILL
DO PREFER MR. BINGLEY

446
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:39,000
TO ANY OTHER MAN I'VE EVER MET.

447
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,000
AND LIZZY...

448
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:43,000
I DID BELIEVE HE...

449
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:45,000
WELL, I WAS
MISTAKEN.

450
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:47,000
THAT IS ALL.

451
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:51,000
I'M RESOLVED
TO THINK OF HIM NO MORE.

452
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:52,000
THERE.

453
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,000
ENOUGH.

454
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
I SHALL BE MYSELF AGAIN

455
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:01,000
AS IF I HAD
NEVER SET EYES ON HIM.

456
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:04,000
TRULY, LIZZY,
I PROMISE I SHALL BE WELL.

457
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,000
I SHALL BE MYSELF AGAIN.

458
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:11,000
I SHALL BE
PERFECTLY CONTENT.

459
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,000
WELL, LIZZY,
WHAT DO YOU THINK NOW

460
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:25,000
ABOUT THIS SAD
BUSINESS OF JANE'S?

461
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:29,000
I CANNOT FIND OUT THAT SHE SAW
ANYTHING OF BINGLEY IN LONDON.

462
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:31,000
WELL...

463
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:34,000
HE'S A VERY
UNDESERVING YOUNG MAN.

464
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:37,000
AND I DON'T SUPPOSE
THERE'S THE LEAST CHANCE

465
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:39,000
OF HER GETTING HIM NOW.

466
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:41,000
IF HE SHOULD COME BACK
TO NETHERFIELD, THOUGH...

467
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:45,000
I THINK THERE'S LITTLE
CHANCE OF THAT, MAMMA.

468
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:47,000
OH, WELL, JUST AS HE CHOOSES.

469
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:50,000
NO ONE WANTS HIM TO COME.

470
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:52,000
OH, I SHALL
ALWAYS SAY

471
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:55,000
HE USED MY DAUGHTER
EXTREMELY ILL.

472
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:57,000
IF I WAS HER, I WOULD
NOT HAVE PUT UP WITH IT.

473
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:00,000
WELL, MY COMFORT
IS SHE WILL DIE
OF A BROKEN HEART

474
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:03,000
AND THEN HE'LL BE SORRY
FOR WHAT HE'S DONE.

475
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:04,000
SO, THE COLLINSES

476
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:08,000
LIVE QUITE COMFORTABLE,
DO THEY?

477
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:10,000
WELL, I ONLY HOPE IT WILL LAST.

478
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:13,000
AND I SUPPOSE THEY TALK
ABOUT HAVING THIS HOUSE, TOO

479
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:15,000
WHEN YOUR FATHER IS DEAD.

480
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:17,000
THEY LOOK ON IT
AS QUITE THEIR OWN

481
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:18,000
I DARESAY.

482
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:20,000
THEY COULD HARDLY DISCUSS

483
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:21,000
SUCH A SUBJECT
IN FRONT OF ME.

484
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,000
WELL, I MAKE NO DOUBT
THEY TALK ABOUT IT CONSTANTLY

485
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:25,000
WHEN THEY'RE ALONE.

486
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:27,000
WELL, IF THEY CAN BE EASY

487
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:30,000
WITH AN ESTATE
THAT IS NOT LAWFULLY THEIR OWN

488
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,000
SO MUCH THE BETTER.

489
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:33,000
I SHOULD BE ASHAMED
OF HAVING ONE

490
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:36,000
THAT WAS ONLY ENTAILED UPON ME.

491
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:37,000
Lydia:
MAMMA!

492
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,000
MAMMA! LIZZY!

493
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:40,000
GUESS WHAT!

494
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:42,000
YOU NEVER WILL,
SO I'LL TELL YOU.

495
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:45,000
MRS. FORSTER HAS INVITED ME
AS HER PARTICULAR FRIEND

496
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:47,000
TO GO WITH HER TO BRIGHTON.

497
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:50,000
COLONEL FORSTER IS TO
TAKE A HOUSE FOR US.

498
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,000
OH, LYDIA!

499
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,000
I AM SO HAPPY!

500
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:55,000
OH, WHAT AN HONOR
TO BE SO SINGLED OUT!

501
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:56,000
IS IT NOT UNFAIR, LIZZY?

502
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,000
MRS. FORSTER SHOULD
HAVE ASKED ME AS WELL.

503
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:00,000
I MAY NOT BE
HER PARTICULAR FRIEND

504
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:03,000
BUT I'VE JUST AS MUCH RIGHT
TO BE ASKED AS SHE HAS.

505
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:04,000
HA, HA, HA!

506
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:09,000
AND MORE, TOO,
FOR I'M TWO YEARS OLDER.

507
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:12,000
Lydia:
WELL, I SHALL BUY HER
A PRESENT, I DARESAY.

508
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,000
WHY BE IN A MIFF

509
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:16,000
BECAUSE MRS. FORSTER
LIKES ME ABOVE ANYONE?

510
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:17,000
BEFORE YOU CROW TOO LOUD

511
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:20,000
REMEMBER PAPA HAS NOT
GIVEN YOU PERMISSION TO GO

512
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,000
AND NOR
IS HE LIKE TO.

513
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:23,000
BUT PAPA
WON'T STOP ME GOING.

514
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:25,000
NOT WHEN I'VE
BEEN SPECIALLY INVITED

515
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:27,000
BY THE COLONEL
OF THE REGIMENT

516
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:29,000
TO BE HIS WIFE'S
PARTICULAR COMPANION.

517
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:31,000
OH, MAMA, I SHALL HAVE
TO BE BOUGHT NEW CLOTHES

518
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
FOR I'VE NOTHING
FIT TO WEAR

519
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,000
AND THERE'LL BE BALLS
AND PARTIES EVERY NIGHT.

520
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:37,000
WELL, OF COURSE YOU
SHALL HAVE NEW THINGS.

521
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:41,000
WE WOULDN'T SEE YOU
DISGRACED IN FRONT
OF ALL THE OFFICERS.

522
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Lydia:
OOH, ALL
THE OFFICERS.

523
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:43,000
OOH!

524
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:44,000
( both giggling )

525
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:47,000
LOOK, I UNDERSTAND
YOUR CONCERN, MY DEAR.

526
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,000
BUT CONSIDER...

527
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:51,000
LYDIA WILL NEVER BE EASY

528
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:53,000
UNTIL SHE HAS EXPOSED HERSELF

529
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,000
IN SOME PUBLIC PLACE

530
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:57,000
AND HERE IS AN OPPORTUNITY
FOR HER TO DO SO

531
00:27:57,000 --> 00:28:00,000
AT VERY LITTLE EXPENSE OR
INCONVENIENCE TO HER FAMILY.

532
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:02,000
IF YOU WERE AWARE, FATHER

533
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:04,000
OF THE VERY GREAT DISADVANTAGE
TO US ALL

534
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:07,000
WHICH MUST ARISE
FROM LYDIA'S IMPRUDENT MANNER--

535
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:09,000
WHICH HAS ALREADY

536
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,000
ARISEN FROM IT,
YOU WOULD JUDGE DIFFERENTLY.

537
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:14,000
HAS SHE FRIGHTENED AWAY
SOME OF YOUR LOVERS?

538
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,000
NOW, DON'T BE
CAST DOWN, LIZZY.

539
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:18,000
SQUEAMISH YOUTHS
ARE NOT WORTH YOUR REGRET.

540
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,000
OH, COME, LIZZY.

541
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:22,000
INDEED, YOU ARE MISTAKEN.

542
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,000
I HAVE NO INJURIES TO RESENT.

543
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:27,000
I SPEAK OF GENERAL,
NOT PARTICULAR EVILS.

544
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:28,000
OUR...

545
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:31,000
POSITION AS A FAMILY,
OUR VERY RESPECTABILITY

546
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:36,000
IS CALLED INTO QUESTION
BY LYDIA'S WILD BEHAVIOR.

547
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:38,000
EXCUSE ME,
I MUST SPEAK PLAINLY.

548
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:41,000
IF YOU DO NOT TAKE
THE TROUBLE TO CHECK HER

549
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:43,000
SHE WILL SOON BE BEYOND
THE REACH OF AMENDMENT.

550
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:47,000
HER CHARACTER WILL BE FIXED
AS THE MOST DETERMINED FLIRT

551
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:50,000
THAT EVER MADE HERSELF
AND HER FAMILY RIDICULOUS.

552
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:52,000
YOU KNOW THAT KITTY
FOLLOWS WHEREVER LYDIA LEADS.

553
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:56,000
DON'T YOU SEE THAT THEY
WILL BE CENSURED AND DESPISED

554
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:57,000
WHEREVER THEY ARE KNOWN?

555
00:28:57,000 --> 00:28:59,000
AND THAT THEY WILL
INVOLVE THEIR SISTERS

556
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:01,000
IN THEIR OWN DISGRACE?

557
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:05,000
LIZZY, LIZZY, COME HERE.

558
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:09,000
DON'T MAKE YOURSELF UNEASY,
MY LOVE.

559
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:11,000
WHEREVER YOU
AND JANE ARE KNOWN

560
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:14,000
YOU MUST BE
RESPECTED AND VALUED.

561
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:18,000
YOU WILL NOT APPEAR TO ANY LESS
ADVANTAGE FOR HAVING A COUPLE

562
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:22,000
OR, IF I MAY SAY,
THREE VERY SILLY SISTERS.

563
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:24,000
WE SHALL HAVE
NO PEACE AT LONGBOURN

564
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:27,000
IF LYDIA DOES
NOT GO TO BRIGHTON.

565
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:30,000
COLONEL FORSTER
IS A SENSIBLE MAN.

566
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:35,000
AND LUCKILY, SHE'S TOO POOR
TO BE AN OBJECT OF PREY

567
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:38,000
TO A FORTUNE HUNTER.

568
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:40,000
NOW, LEAVE IT NOW, LIZZY.

569
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:45,000
I BELIEVE
ALL WILL TURN OUT WELL.

570
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:51,000
( lively conversation )

571
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:54,000
WE ARE SO DESOLATED, COLONEL

572
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,000
THAT THE REGIMENT
IS TO LEAVE MERYTON.

573
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:58,000
BUT WORDS CANNOT EXPRESS

574
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:01,000
WHAT WE FEEL ABOUT
YOUR KINDNESS TO OUR DEAR LYDIA.

575
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:02,000
WELL, MA'AM, IT APPEARS

576
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:05,000
THAT MRS. FORSTER
CANNOT DO WITHOUT HER.

577
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:06,000
( women laughing )

578
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:07,000
LOOK AT THE PAIR OF THEM.

579
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:08,000
THICK AS THIEVES.

580
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:11,000
LORD KNOWS WHAT
THEY FIND TO TALK ABOUT.

581
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,000
BUT ANYTHING
TO KEEP THE LADIES HAPPY.

582
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:16,000
WHAT DO YOU SAY,
WICKHAM?

583
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:21,000
I SAY AMEN
TO THAT, SIR.

584
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:29,000
THERE'S ONE LADY I SHALL
BE VERY LOATH TO PART FROM.

585
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:31,000
WELL, WE MUST BEAR IT
AS BEST WE CAN.

586
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:33,000
YOU ARE FOR BRIGHTON;

587
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:36,000
I SHALL BE TOURING THE LAKES
WITH MY AUNT AND UNCLE.

588
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:38,000
I DARESAY WE SHALL
FIND AMPLE SOURCES

589
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:41,000
OF CONSOLATION AND DELIGHT
IN OUR DIFFERENT WAYS.

590
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,000
PERHAPS.

591
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:44,000
HOW DID YOU FIND ROSINGS?

592
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:46,000
VERY INTERESTING.

593
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:48,000
COLONEL FITZWILLIAM
WAS THERE WITH MR. DARCY.

594
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:50,000
ARE YOU AT ALL ACQUAINTED
WITH THE COLONEL?

595
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:52,000
I, UM...

596
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:55,000
TO SOME RESPECTS,
YES, IN FORMER YEARS.

597
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:57,000
VERY GENTLEMANLY MAN.

598
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:58,000
HOW DID
YOU LIKE HIM?

599
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,000
I LIKED HIM VERY MUCH INDEED.

600
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:04,000
HIS MANNERS ARE VERY DIFFERENT
FROM HIS COUSIN'S.

601
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:06,000
YES.

602
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:09,000
BUT I THINK MR. DARCY IMPROVES

603
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:11,000
ON CLOSER
ACQUAINTANCE.

604
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:13,000
INDEED?

605
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:15,000
IN WHAT RESPECT?

606
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:19,000
HAS HE ACQUIRED A TOUCH
OF CIVILITY IN HIS ADDRESS?

607
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:22,000
FOR I DARE NOT HOPE HE HAS
IMPROVED IN ESSENTIALS.

608
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:23,000
NO.

609
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:28,000
IN ESSENTIALS, I BELIEVE HE
IS VERY MUCH AS HE EVER WAS.

610
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:30,000
AH.

611
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:33,000
I DON'T MEAN TO IMPLY

612
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:37,000
THAT EITHER HIS MIND
OR HIS MANNERS ARE CHANGED

613
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:38,000
FOR THE BETTER.

614
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:41,000
RATHER, MY KNOWING HIM BETTER

615
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:43,000
IMPROVED MY OPINION OF HIM.

616
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:45,000
I SEE.

617
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,000
Mrs. Forster:
WICKHAM?

618
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:48,000
WICKHAM?

619
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:51,000
COME HERE.

620
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,000
AT YOUR SERVICE, MA'AM.

621
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:56,000
YES, GO, GO.

622
00:31:56,000 --> 00:32:01,000
I WOULD NOT WISH YOU BACK AGAIN.

623
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,000
BYE, PAPA, BYE, MAMMA.

624
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:09,000
OH, LYDIA, MY DEAR,
WE SHALL MISS YOU MOST CRUELLY.

625
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:11,000
WELL, I SHALL WRITE
EVERY DAY WHAT I AM DOING

626
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:14,000
AND MAKE YOU
WILD WITH ENVY.

627
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,000
I CAN'T HELP IT.

628
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:17,000
I SHALL NOT
ENVY HER A JOT.

629
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:19,000
WELL, I MUST GO.

630
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:21,000
GOOD-BYE, JANE,
GOOD-BYE, LIZZY.

631
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:23,000
IF I SEE ANY
ELIGIBLE BEAUS FOR YOU

632
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:24,000
I'LL SEND YOU
WORD EXPRESS.

633
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:26,000
OH, LORD,
WHAT A LAUGH

634
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:28,000
IF I SHOULD FALL
AND BREAK MY HEAD.

635
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:29,000
I WISH
SHE WOULD.

636
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:31,000
OH, MY DEAR GIRL.

637
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:35,000
TAKE EVERY OPPORTUNITY
OF ENJOYING YOURSELF.

638
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:40,000
BYE, BYE.

639
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:53,000
( crying )

640
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:55,000
WELL, NEVER MIND,
KITTY.

641
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:57,000
I DARESAY,
IN A YEAR OR TWO

642
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:59,000
YOU'LL HAVE GOT OVER
IT TOLERABLY WELL.

643
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:01,000
( sobbing )

644
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:02,000
IF ANYONE
SHOULD ASK FOR ME

645
00:33:02,000 --> 00:33:04,000
I SHALL BE
IN MY LIBRARY

646
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:09,000
AND NOT
TO BE DISTURBED.

647
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:27,000
HELLO! I CAN SEE...

648
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,000
I CAN SEE ALICIA--

649
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:31,000
LOOK HOW SHE'S GROWN!

650
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:32,000
HELLO!

651
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,000
OH!

652
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:35,000
YOU MUST BE SO TIRED.

653
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,000
HELLO.
HELLO, ALICIA.

654
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,000
( clamoring greetings )

655
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:39,000
HOW HAVE YOU ALL GROWN!

656
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:41,000
I THINK
YOU'VE ALL GROWN

657
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:42,000
SINCE WE LAST
SAID GOOD-BYE!

658
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:43,000
AND VERY
PRETTILY, TOO.

659
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,000
COME INTO
THE HOUSE THEN.

660
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:48,000
SUCH A SWEET,
STEADY GIRL.

661
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:49,000
OH, LIZZY!

662
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:51,000
OH!

663
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:53,000
WE BEAR YOU
BAD TIDINGS.

664
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:55,000
NOT TOO GRIEVOUS,
THOUGH, I HOPE.

665
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:56,000
THE GUILT IS MINE.

666
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:58,000
MY BUSINESS WON'T
ALLOW ME TIME AWAY

667
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:00,000
TO VISIT ALL
THE LAKE COUNTRY.

668
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,000
WE SHALL HAVE TO CONTENT
OURSELVES WITH DERBYSHIRE.

669
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:04,000
OH.

670
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:06,000
BUT DERBYSHIRE
HAS MANY BEAUTIES

671
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:07,000
HAS IT NOT?

672
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:09,000
INDEED, TO ME

673
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:11,000
DERBYSHIRE IS THE BEST
OF ALL COUNTIES.

674
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:12,000
YOU WILL JUDGE
FOR YOURSELF

675
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:14,000
WHETHER CHATSWORTH

676
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,000
IS NOT THE EQUAL
OF BLENHAM.

677
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:17,000
AND SURELY
THE SOUTHERN COUNTIES

678
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:19,000
HAVE NOTHING
TO COMPARE TO THE WILD

679
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:24,000
AND UNTAMED BEAUTY
OF THE PEAKS.

680
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Mr. Gardiner:
NATURE AND CULTURE IN HARMONY,
YOU SEE, LIZZY

681
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:33,000
WILDNESS AND ARTIFICE--

682
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:35,000
AND ALL
IN THE ONE PERFECT COUNTY!

683
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:38,000
Mrs. Gardiner:
WELL, I WAS BORN
AND GREW UP HERE

684
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:40,000
SO I SHOULD NEVER DISAGREE
WITH THAT.

685
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Lizzy:
WHERE, EXACTLY?

686
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:43,000
AT LAMBTON,
A LITTLE TOWN

687
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,000
OF NO CONSEQUENCE
EXCEPT TO THOSE

688
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:47,000
FORTUNATE ENOUGH
TO HAVE LIVED IN IT.

689
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:49,000
I THINK IT
THE DEAREST PLACE

690
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,000
IN THE WORLD.

691
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:53,000
THEN I SHALL NOT BE HAPPY
TILL I HAVE SEEN IT.

692
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:56,000
IT HAS ONE FURTHER CLAIM
ON YOUR INTEREST:

693
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:58,000
IT IS BUT FIVE MILES
FROM PEMBERLEY

694
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:00,000
AND OWES MUCH
OF ITS PROSPERITY

695
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,000
TO THAT GREAT ESTATE.

696
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,000
SO NEAR?

697
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:05,000
NOT THAT I OR ANY
OF MY ACQUAINTANCE

698
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:07,000
ENJOYED THE PRIVILEGE
OF INTIMACY

699
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:09,000
WITH THAT FAMILY.

700
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:14,000
WE MOVED IN VERY
DIFFERENT CIRCLES.

701
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,000
A HIT, ACKNOWLEDGED.

702
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:26,000
VERY GOOD, SIR!

703
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:27,000
ENOUGH, SIR?

704
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:29,000
ENOUGH.
THANK YOU, BAINES.

705
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:32,000
WILL YOU COME AGAIN TOMORROW,
SIR, AT 10:00?

706
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:34,000
NOT TOMORROW,
I HAVE BUSINESS IN THE NORTH.

707
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,000
I'LL COME BACK TOMORROW WEEK.

708
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,000
VERY GOOD, SIR.

709
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,000
BID YOU GOOD DAY, SIR.

710
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:39,000
THANK YOU, BAINES.

711
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:43,000
GOOD DAY.

712
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:45,000
I SHALL CONQUER THIS.

713
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:47,000
I SHALL.

714
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:52,000
( hawk crying )

715
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:58,000
( hawks crying )

716
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Mrs. Gardiner:
ELIZABETH, BE CAREFUL!

717
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:06,000
HOW COULD I FACE YOUR FATHER
IF YOU TOOK A FALL?

718
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:12,000
BEAUTIFUL!

719
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:17,000
( hawk crying )

720
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:19,000
THANK YOU, HANNAH.

721
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:22,000
YOU'RE WELCOME, SIR.

722
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,000
( sighs )

723
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,000
I THINK I SHOULD
BE QUITE HAPPY

724
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:27,000
TO STAY MY WHOLE LIFE
IN DERBYSHIRE.

725
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:28,000
I'M HAPPY
TO HEAR IT.

726
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,000
NOW, WHAT DO YOU SAY

727
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:31,000
TO VISITING
PEMBERLEY TOMORROW?

728
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:33,000
IT'S NOT DIRECTLY
IN OUR WAY

729
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:35,000
BUT NO MORE
THAN A MILE OR TWO

730
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,000
OUT OF IT.

731
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,000
DO YOU ESPECIALLY WISH
TO SEE IT, AUNT?

732
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:40,000
I SHOULD HAVE THOUGHT
YOU WOULD

733
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:42,000
HAVING HEARD SO MUCH
ABOUT IT.

734
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:45,000
AND THE ASSOCIATIONS
ARE NOT ALL UNPLEASANT.

735
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:46,000
WICKHAM PASSED
HIS YOUTH THERE.

736
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:48,000
WE HAVE NO BUSINESS THERE.

737
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,000
I SHOULD FEEL AWKWARD

738
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:52,000
TO VISIT THE PLACE
WITHOUT A PROPER INVITATION.

739
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:54,000
NO MORE THAN BLENHAM
OR CHATSWORTH.

740
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:56,000
THERE WAS
NO AWKWARDNESS THERE.

741
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:58,000
I SHOULDN'T CARE FOR IT
MYSELF, LIZZY

742
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:00,000
IF IT WERE MERELY
A FINE HOUSE

743
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:01,000
RICHLY FURNISHED

744
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:03,000
BUT THE GROUNDS
ARE DELIGHTFUL.

745
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:05,000
THEY HAVE SOME
OF THE FINEST WOODS

746
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:06,000
IN THE COUNTRY.

747
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:09,000
HOW FAR ARE WE FROM
PEMBERLEY, MY DEAR?

748
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:10,000
NOT MORE THAN
FIVE MILES, SIR.

749
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:13,000
THE GROUNDS
ARE VERY FINE,
ARE THEY NOT?

750
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:15,000
AS FINE AS YOU'LL SEE
ANYWHERE, MA'AM.

751
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:19,000
MY OLDEST BROTHER IS
AN UNDER-GARDENER THERE.

752
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:21,000
IS THE FAMILY HERE
FOR THE SUMMER?

753
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:24,000
NO, MA'AM.

754
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:29,000
WELL?

755
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:34,000
PERHAPS WE MIGHT VISIT PEMBERLEY
AFTER ALL.

756
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:03,000
( birds singing )

757
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Mr. Gardiner:
I THINK WE'VE SEEN
WOODS AND GROVES ENOUGH

758
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:08,000
TO SATISFY EVEN YOUR ENTHUSIASM
FOR THEM, LIZZY.

759
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:10,000
I CONFESS I HAD NO IDEA

760
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,000
PEMBERLEY WAS SUCH
A GREAT ESTATE.

761
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:14,000
SHALL WE REACH
THE HOUSE ITSELF

762
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,000
BEFORE DARK,
DO YOU THINK?

763
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:20,000
BE PATIENT, WAIT.

764
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:23,000
THERE.

765
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:27,000
Mr. Gardiner:
STOP THE COACH.

766
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,000
( sighs )

767
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:30,000
I THINK ONE
WOULD BE WILLING

768
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:32,000
TO PUT UP WITH
A GOOD DEAL

769
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:33,000
TO BE MISTRESS
OF PEMBERLEY.

770
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:35,000
THE MISTRESS OF PEMBERLEY

771
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:38,000
WILL HAVE TO PUT UP
WITH A GOOD DEAL.

772
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:42,000
SHE'S NOT LIKELY TO BE
ANYONE WE KNOW.

773
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:45,000
HOW DO YOU LIKE
THE HOUSE, LIZZY?

774
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:46,000
VERY WELL.

775
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:49,000
I DON'T THINK
I'VE EVER SEEN

776
00:38:49,000 --> 00:38:52,000
A PLACE SO HAPPILY SITUATED.

777
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:56,000
I LIKE IT VERY WELL INDEED.

778
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:57,000
Mr. Gardiner:
DRIVE ON.

779
00:38:57,000 --> 00:39:00,000
PITY THEN ITS OWNER SHOULD BE

780
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:02,000
SUCH A PROUD
AND DISAGREEABLE MAN.

781
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:07,000
YES, A GREAT PITY.

782
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:09,000
PERHAPS THE BEAUTY
OF THE HOUSE

783
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:10,000
RENDERS ITS OWNER

784
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:12,000
A LITTLE LESS
REPULSIVE, LIZZY?

785
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,000
YES, PERHAPS.

786
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:15,000
( chuckles )

787
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:19,000
PERHAPS A VERY LITTLE.

788
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:20,000
WELL...

789
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:22,000
SHALL WE APPLY
TO THE HOUSEKEEPER

790
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:27,000
TO SEE INSIDE THE PLACE?

791
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:41,000
THAT'S WHERE
MRS. DARCY

792
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:43,000
USED TO WRITE
HER LETTERS

793
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:44,000
EVERY MORNING.

794
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:49,000
IT WAS HER
FAVORITE ROOM.

795
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:53,000
THIS IS THE MUSIC ROOM.

796
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:55,000
( gasps softly )

797
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:56,000
Mrs. Gardiner:
CHARMING.

798
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:59,000
Mr. Gardiner:
WHAT A LOVELY ROOM
THIS IS.

799
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Mrs. Gardiner:
DELIGHTFUL.

800
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:03,000
( clock chiming  )

801
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:05,000
AND THERE'S
A FINE PROSPECT

802
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:09,000
FROM THAT WINDOW
DOWN TOWARDS THE LAKE.

803
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:11,000
Mrs. Gardiner:
LOOK AT THIS,
MY DEAR.

804
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:16,000
Mr. Gardiner:
OH, IT'S QUITE
MAGNIFICENT.

805
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:18,000
( bird cawing )

806
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:20,000
OF ALL THIS,
I MIGHT HAVE BEEN MISTRESS.

807
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:23,000
Housekeeper:
THIS PIANO HAS
JUST COME DOWN.

808
00:40:23,000 --> 00:40:26,000
IT'S A PRESENT FROM MY MASTER
FOR MISS GEORGIANA.

809
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:28,000
YOUR MASTER
IS FROM HOME,
WE UNDERSTAND.

810
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:31,000
YES, BUT WE EXPECT HIM
HERE TOMORROW, SIR.

811
00:40:31,000 --> 00:40:35,000
HE IS COMING WITH
A LARGE PARTY OF FRIENDS

812
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:39,000
AND MISS GEORGIANA.

813
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:42,000
THIS PORTRAIT WAS PAINTED
EARLIER THIS YEAR

814
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:44,000
FOR HER 16th BIRTHDAY.

815
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:47,000
AH! SHE IS A VERY
HANDSOME YOUNG LADY.

816
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:49,000
OH, YES!

817
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:50,000
THE HANDSOMEST
YOUNG LADY

818
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:51,000
THAT EVER WAS SEEN.

819
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:53,000
AND SO ACCOMPLISHED--

820
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:57,000
SHE PLAYS AND SINGS
ALL DAY LONG!

821
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:58,000
LIZZY.

822
00:40:58,000 --> 00:41:03,000
LOOK AT THIS PICTURE!

823
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:06,000
IT REMINDS ME VERY MUCH
OF SOMEONE WE KNOW!

824
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:08,000
THIS ONE,
MA'AM?

825
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:10,000
THAT YOUNG
GENTLEMAN
WAS THE SON

826
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:12,000
OF THE LATE
MR. DARCY'S STEWARD

827
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:13,000
MR. WICKHAM.

828
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:15,000
HE IS GONE INTO
THE ARMY NOW--

829
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:17,000
BUT HE'S TURNED OUT
VERY WILD.

830
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:20,000
VERY WILD INDEED,
I'M AFRAID.

831
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:21,000
THAT'S
MY MASTER

832
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:23,000
AND VERY
LIKE HIM, TOO.

833
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:25,000
Mrs. Gardiner:
IT IS A HANDSOME FACE--

834
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:27,000
BUT I'VE NEVER
SEEN THE ORIGINAL.

835
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:29,000
IS IT LIKE
HIM, LIZZY?

836
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:31,000
OH! DOES THIS
YOUNG LADY

837
00:41:31,000 --> 00:41:32,000
KNOW THE MASTER?

838
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:33,000
YES, A LITTLE.

839
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:36,000
OH, AND HE IS
A HANDSOME GENTLEMAN

840
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:37,000
IS HE NOT, MA'AM?

841
00:41:37,000 --> 00:41:39,000
YES, VERY
HANDSOME.

842
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:40,000
MM. I'M SURE

843
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:42,000
I KNOW NONE
SO HANDSOME.

844
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:43,000
NOR SO KIND.

845
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:44,000
Mr. Gardiner:
INDEED?

846
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:46,000
AYE, SIR, I'VE NEVER

847
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:48,000
HAD A CROSS WORD
FROM HIM IN MY LIFE.

848
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:49,000
AND I'VE
KNOWN HIM

849
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:51,000
SINCE HE WAS
FOUR YEARS OLD.

850
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,000
BUT THEN I'VE
ALWAYS OBSERVED

851
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:54,000
THAT THEY THAT
ARE GOOD-NATURED

852
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:55,000
WHEN THEY
ARE CHILDREN

853
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:57,000
ARE GOOD-NATURED
WHEN THEY GROW UP.

854
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:59,000
HIS FATHER WAS
AN EXCELLENT MAN.

855
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:00,000
HE WAS, MA'AM

856
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:03,000
AND HIS SON WILL
BE JUST LIKE HIM--

857
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:06,000
THE BEST LANDLORD
AND THE BEST MASTER.

858
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,000
ASK ANY
OF HIS TENANTS

859
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:08,000
OR HIS SERVANTS.

860
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:11,000
SOME PEOPLE
CALL HIM PROUD

861
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:13,000
BUT I FANCY THAT'S

862
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:15,000
ONLY BECAUSE HE
DON'T RATTLE AWAY

863
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:17,000
LIKE OTHER
YOUNG MEN DO.

864
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:18,000
NOW, IF YOU
WILL FOLLOW ME

865
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:20,000
THERE'S A FINER,
LARGER PORTRAIT

866
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:22,000
OF HIM IN THE GALLERY
UPSTAIRS.

867
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:23,000
THIS WAY, SIR

868
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:25,000
IF YOU PLEASE.

869
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,000
THIS FINE ACCOUNT
OF DARCY

870
00:42:26,000 --> 00:42:27,000
IS NOT QUITE
CONSISTENT

871
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:29,000
WITH HIS BEHAVIOR
TO POOR WICKHAM.

872
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:32,000
PERHAPS WE MIGHT HAVE
BEEN DECEIVED THERE.

873
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:36,000
THAT'S NOT LIKELY,
IS IT?

874
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:41,000
( birds twittering )

875
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:31,000
AH...

876
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:36,000
MAGNIFICENT.

877
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:50,000
Housekeeper:
THERE.

878
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:03,000
WOULD YOU NOT LIKE
TO RIDE HIM, SIR?

879
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:08,000
NO, NO, NO, TAKE HIM
BACK TO THE STABLES.

880
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:40,000
MR. DARCY!

881
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:41,000
MISS BENNET.

882
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:43,000
I...

883
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:45,000
I DID NOT EXPECT
TO SEE YOU, SIR.

884
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:47,000
WE UNDERSTOOD
ALL THE FAMILY WERE FROM HOME

885
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:49,000
OR WE SHOULD
NEVER HAVE PRESUMED...

886
00:45:49,000 --> 00:45:51,000
I RETURNED A DAY EARLY.

887
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:52,000
EXCUSE ME.

888
00:45:52,000 --> 00:45:55,000
YOUR PARENTS ARE IN GOOD HEALTH?

889
00:45:55,000 --> 00:45:56,000
UH, YES.

890
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:57,000
THEY ARE VERY WELL.

891
00:45:57,000 --> 00:45:59,000
I THANK YOU, SIR.

892
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:01,000
I'M GLAD TO HEAR IT.

893
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:04,000
HOW LONG HAVE YOU BEEN
IN THIS PART OF THE COUNTRY?

894
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:07,000
BUT TWO DAYS, SIR.

895
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:09,000
AND WHERE ARE YOU STAYING?

896
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:11,000
AT THE INN AT LAMBTON.

897
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:13,000
OH, YES, OF COURSE.

898
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:14,000
MM...

899
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:18,000
WELL, I'M... I'M
JUST ARRIVED MYSELF.

900
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:20,000
AND YOUR PARENTS
ARE IN GOOD HEALTH?

901
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:22,000
AND ALL YOUR SISTERS?

902
00:46:22,000 --> 00:46:23,000
YES.

903
00:46:23,000 --> 00:46:28,000
THEY'RE ALL
IN EXCELLENT HEALTH, SIR.

904
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:33,000
EXCUSE ME.

905
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:41,000
THE MAN HIMSELF,
I PRESUME.

906
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:43,000
JUST AS HANDSOME
AS IN HIS PORTRAIT.

907
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:45,000
THOUGH PERHAPS A LITTLE
LESS FORMALLY ATTIRED.

908
00:46:45,000 --> 00:46:47,000
WE MUST LEAVE
HERE AT ONCE.

909
00:46:47,000 --> 00:46:49,000
WHY, OF COURSE,
IF YOU WISH.

910
00:46:49,000 --> 00:46:51,000
OH, I WISH
WE'D NEVER COME.

911
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:53,000
WHAT MUST HE
THINK OF ME?

912
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:54,000
WAS HE DISPLEASED?

913
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:55,000
WHAT DID HE SAY?

914
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:56,000
NOTHING
OF CONSEQUENCE.

915
00:46:56,000 --> 00:47:01,000
HE ENQUIRED
AFTER MY PARENTS...

916
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:17,000
MISS BENNET,
PLEASE ALLOW ME

917
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:19,000
TO APOLOGIZE
FOR NOT RECEIVING YOU

918
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:20,000
PROPERLY JUST NOW.

919
00:47:20,000 --> 00:47:22,000
YOU ARE NOT LEAVING?

920
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:24,000
WE WERE, SIR, I THINK WE MUST.

921
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:27,000
I HOPE YOU'RE
NOT DISPLEASED

922
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:29,000
WITH PEMBERLEY.

923
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:30,000
NO, NOT AT ALL.

924
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:32,000
THEN YOU APPROVE OF IT?

925
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:34,000
VERY MUCH.

926
00:47:34,000 --> 00:47:37,000
BUT I THINK THERE ARE
FEW WHO WOULD NOT APPROVE.

927
00:47:37,000 --> 00:47:39,000
BUT YOUR GOOD OPINION
IS RARELY BESTOWED

928
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:41,000
AND MORE WORTH EARNING.

929
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:42,000
THANK YOU.

930
00:47:42,000 --> 00:47:44,000
WOULD YOU DO ME THE HONOR

931
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:46,000
OF INTRODUCING ME
TO YOUR FRIENDS?

932
00:47:46,000 --> 00:47:48,000
CERTAINLY.

933
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:51,000
MR. AND MRS. EDWARD GARDINER,
MR. DARCY.

934
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:53,000
MRS. GARDINER
IS MY AUNT, MR. DARCY

935
00:47:53,000 --> 00:47:56,000
MY SISTER JANE STAYED AT
THEIR HOUSE IN CHEAPSIDE

936
00:47:56,000 --> 00:47:57,000
WHEN SHE WAS
LATELY IN LONDON.

937
00:47:57,000 --> 00:48:00,000
DELIGHTED TO MAKE YOUR
ACQUAINTANCE, MADAM.

938
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:01,000
DELIGHTED, SIR.

939
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:02,000
YOU'RE STAYING
IN LAMBTON?

940
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:05,000
YES, SIR, I GREW UP
THERE AS A GIRL.

941
00:48:05,000 --> 00:48:06,000
DELIGHTFUL VILLAGE.

942
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:07,000
I REMEMBER RUNNING

943
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:08,000
FROM PEMBERLEY
TO LAMBTON AS A BOY

944
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:11,000
ALMOST EVERY DAY
IN THE HORSE CHESTNUT SEASON.

945
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:13,000
THERE WAS ONE
VERY FINE TREE THERE...

946
00:48:13,000 --> 00:48:14,000
ON THE GREEN,
BY THE SMITHY.

947
00:48:14,000 --> 00:48:15,000
THE VERY ONE.

948
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:18,000
MR. GARDINER,
DO YOU CARE FOR FISHING?

949
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:21,000
INDEED, I DO, SIR,
WHEN I GET THE CHANCE OF IT.

950
00:48:21,000 --> 00:48:23,000
YOU MUST COME AND FISH
IN MY TROUT STREAM.

951
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:25,000
OR THERE ARE CARP,
TENCH AND PIKE

952
00:48:25,000 --> 00:48:27,000
IF YOUR BENT RUNS
TO COARSE FISHING.

953
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:29,000
I COULD PROVIDE YOU
WITH RODS AND TACKLE

954
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:30,000
SHOW YOU THE BEST SPOTS.

955
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:32,000
LET US WALK DOWN NOW.

956
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:34,000
FOLLOW US TO THE LAKE,
MY MAN WILL SHOW YOU.

957
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:38,000
THERE'S A PLACE DOWN
THERE WHERE WE USED
TO TICKLE THEM OUT...

958
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:41,000
IS THIS THE PROUD DARCY
YOU TOLD US OF?

959
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:43,000
HE IS ALL EASE
AND FRIENDLINESS

960
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:44,000
NO FALSE DIGNITY
AT ALL.

961
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:46,000
I'M AS ASTONISHED
AS YOU ARE.

962
00:48:46,000 --> 00:48:49,000
I CAN'T IMAGINE WHAT
HAS AFFECTED THIS
TRANSFORMATION.

963
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:54,000
CAN YOU NOT?

964
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:11,000
Darcy:
DO YOU...

965
00:49:11,000 --> 00:49:12,000
Lizzy:
UH...

966
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:13,000
Darcy:
PRAY, CONTINUE.

967
00:49:13,000 --> 00:49:16,000
I WAS GOING
TO SAY AGAIN, SIR

968
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:19,000
HOW VERY UNEXPECTED
YOUR ARRIVAL WAS.

969
00:49:19,000 --> 00:49:21,000
IF WE HAD KNOWN
YOU WERE TO BE HERE

970
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:24,000
WE SHOULD NOT HAVE DREAMT
OF INVADING YOUR PRIVACY.

971
00:49:24,000 --> 00:49:25,000
THE HOUSEKEEPER ASSURED US

972
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:28,000
YOU WOULD NOT BE HERE
UNTIL TOMORROW.

973
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:30,000
I BEG YOU, DO NOT
MAKE YOURSELF UNEASY.

974
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:31,000
I HAD PLANNED IT SO MYSELF.

975
00:49:31,000 --> 00:49:33,000
BUT I FOUND I HAD BUSINESS
WITH MY STEWARD

976
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:36,000
AND SO RODE AHEAD
OF THE REST OF THE PARTY

977
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:37,000
WITHOUT
INFORMING ANYONE.

978
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:39,000
THEY WILL
JOIN ME TOMORROW.

979
00:49:39,000 --> 00:49:41,000
AND AMONG THEM
ARE THOSE

980
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:45,000
WHO CLAIM
AN ACQUAINTANCE WITH YOU.

981
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:50,000
IT'S MR. BINGLEY
AND HIS SISTERS.

982
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:53,000
OH.

983
00:49:53,000 --> 00:49:55,000
THERE'S THE OTHER PERSON
IN THE PARTY

984
00:49:55,000 --> 00:50:00,000
WHO MORE PARTICULARLY
WISHES TO KNOW YOU.

985
00:50:01,000 --> 00:50:03,000
WILL YOU ALLOW ME TO...

986
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:06,000
DO I ASK TOO MUCH
TO INTRODUCE MY
SISTER TO YOU

987
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:10,000
DURING YOUR STAY
AT LAMBTON?

988
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:15,000
I SHOULD BE VERY HAPPY
TO MAKE HER ACQUAINTANCE.

989
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:20,000
THANK YOU.

990
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:34,000
THANK YOU.

991
00:50:34,000 --> 00:50:36,000
I HOPE WE SHALL
MEET AGAIN VERY SOON.

992
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:39,000
GOOD DAY, MR. GARDINER.

993
00:50:39,000 --> 00:50:40,000
MRS. GARDINER.

994
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:45,000
GOOD DAY, MISS BENNET.

995
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:18,000
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH
IF YOU PLEASE, MA'AM.

996
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:21,000
THERE'S TWO GENTLEMEN
AND A LADY

997
00:51:21,000 --> 00:51:23,000
WAITING UPON YOU
IN THE PARLOR.

998
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:27,000
ONE OF THE GENTLEMEN
IS MR. DARCY.

999
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:29,000
THANK YOU.

1000
00:51:29,000 --> 00:51:34,000
TELL THEM I SHALL
COME DIRECTLY.

1001
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:46,000
MR. DARCY.

1002
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:49,000
I HOPE THAT YOU HAVE
NOT BEEN WAITING LONG.

1003
00:51:49,000 --> 00:51:51,000
NOT AT ALL.

1004
00:51:51,000 --> 00:51:56,000
MAY I INTRODUCE
MY SISTER GEORGIANA?

1005
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:04,000
GEORGIANA, THIS IS
MISS ELIZABETH BENNET.

1006
00:52:04,000 --> 00:52:05,000
HOW DO YOU DO?

1007
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:07,000
I'M VERY PLEASED
TO MEET YOU, MISS DARCY.

1008
00:52:07,000 --> 00:52:09,000
I'VE HEARD
SO MUCH ABOUT YOU.

1009
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:11,000
AND I ABOUT YOU.

1010
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:12,000
MR. BINGLEY IS
HERE WITH US

1011
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:14,000
AND VERY DESIROUS
TO SEE YOU AS WELL.

1012
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:16,000
HE INSISTED ON ACCOMPANYING US.

1013
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:17,000
MAY I SUMMON HIM?

1014
00:52:17,000 --> 00:52:18,000
OF COURSE.

1015
00:52:18,000 --> 00:52:20,000
I SHOULD LIKE

1016
00:52:20,000 --> 00:52:25,000
TO SEE HIM
VERY MUCH.

1017
00:52:25,000 --> 00:52:27,000
I UNDERSTAND

1018
00:52:27,000 --> 00:52:29,000
THAT YOU ARE FOND OF MUSIC

1019
00:52:29,000 --> 00:52:31,000
AND PLAY VERY WELL.

1020
00:52:31,000 --> 00:52:33,000
OH, NO. NOT
PLAY VERY WELL.

1021
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:36,000
I MEAN, BUT I AM
VERY FOND OF MUSIC.

1022
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:39,000
I SHOULD DEARLY LOVE
TO HEAR YOU PLAY AND SING.

1023
00:52:39,000 --> 00:52:41,000
MY BROTHER HAS TOLD ME

1024
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:42,000
HE HAS RARELY
HEARD ANYTHING

1025
00:52:42,000 --> 00:52:44,000
THAT GAVE HIM
MORE PLEASURE.

1026
00:52:44,000 --> 00:52:46,000
WELL, YOU SHALL,
BUT I WARN YOU

1027
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:49,000
YOUR BROTHER HAS GROSSLY
EXAGGERATED MY TALENTS.

1028
00:52:49,000 --> 00:52:53,000
NO DOUBT FOR SOME MISCHIEVOUS
REASON OF HIS OWN.

1029
00:52:53,000 --> 00:52:55,000
OH, NO. THAT
COULD NOT BE SO.

1030
00:52:55,000 --> 00:52:57,000
MY BROTHER NEVER
EXAGGERATES.

1031
00:52:57,000 --> 00:52:59,000
HE ALWAYS TELLS
THE ABSOLUTE TRUTH

1032
00:52:59,000 --> 00:53:01,000
EXCEPT THAT SOMETIMES

1033
00:53:01,000 --> 00:53:04,000
I THINK HE IS
A LITTLE TOO KIND TO ME.

1034
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:06,000
AN IDEAL ELDER BROTHER THEN.

1035
00:53:06,000 --> 00:53:08,000
OH, YES. I
COULD NOT IMAGINE

1036
00:53:08,000 --> 00:53:10,000
A BETTER OR
A KINDER ONE.

1037
00:53:10,000 --> 00:53:12,000
YOU MAKE ME FEEL QUITE ENVIOUS.

1038
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:15,000
I HAVE NO BROTHERS AT ALL,
ONLY FOUR SISTERS.

1039
00:53:15,000 --> 00:53:17,000
I SHOULD HAVE LIKED
TO HAVE A SISTER.

1040
00:53:17,000 --> 00:53:19,000
( footsteps approaching )

1041
00:53:19,000 --> 00:53:21,000
MISS BENNET

1042
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:23,000
I CAN'T TELL YOU
HOW DELIGHTED I WAS

1043
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:27,000
WHEN DARCY TOLD ME YOU WERE
NOT FIVE MILES FROM PEMBERLEY.

1044
00:53:27,000 --> 00:53:28,000
HOW DO YOU DO?

1045
00:53:28,000 --> 00:53:29,000
BUT I CAN SEE
THAT YOU'RE WELL.

1046
00:53:29,000 --> 00:53:31,000
VERY WELL INDEED,
THANK YOU.

1047
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:32,000
GOOD. GOOD. EXCELLENT.

1048
00:53:32,000 --> 00:53:33,000
AND YOUR FAMILY?

1049
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:35,000
VERY WELL, SIR.

1050
00:53:35,000 --> 00:53:38,000
YES?

1051
00:53:38,000 --> 00:53:42,000
PRAY TELL ME, ARE ALL
YOUR SISTERS STILL AT LONGBOURN?

1052
00:53:42,000 --> 00:53:43,000
ALL EXCEPT ONE.

1053
00:53:43,000 --> 00:53:46,000
MY YOUNGEST SISTER
IS AT BRIGHTON.

1054
00:53:46,000 --> 00:53:50,000
AH.

1055
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:52,000
IT SEEMS TOO LONG...

1056
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:54,000
IT IS TOO LONG
SINCE I HAD

1057
00:53:54,000 --> 00:53:56,000
THE PLEASURE
OF SPEAKING TO YOU.

1058
00:53:56,000 --> 00:53:57,000
IT MUST BE
SEVERAL MONTHS.

1059
00:53:57,000 --> 00:54:00,000
IT IS ABOVE EIGHT
MONTHS AT LEAST.

1060
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:02,000
WE HAVE NOT MET SINCE
THE 26th OF NOVEMBER

1061
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:05,000
WHEN WE WERE DANCING
TOGETHER AT NETHERFIELD.

1062
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:08,000
I THINK YOU MUST BE RIGHT.

1063
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:11,000
I DON'T THINK
I CAN REMEMBER A HAPPIER TIME

1064
00:54:11,000 --> 00:54:12,000
THAN THOSE SHORT MONTHS

1065
00:54:12,000 --> 00:54:14,000
I SPENT IN
HERTFORDSHIRE.

1066
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:15,000
Darcy:
MISS BENNET.

1067
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:19,000
MY SISTER HAS A REQUEST
TO MAKE OF YOU.

1068
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:23,000
MISS BENNET, MY BROTHER AND I
WOULD BE HONORED

1069
00:54:23,000 --> 00:54:26,000
IF YOU AND YOUR AUNT AND UNCLE

1070
00:54:26,000 --> 00:54:30,000
WOULD BE OUR GUESTS
AT PEMBERLEY FOR DINNER.

1071
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:32,000
WOULD TOMORROW EVENING
BE CONVENIENT?

1072
00:54:32,000 --> 00:54:35,000
THANK YOU.
WE SHALL BE DELIGHTED.

1073
00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:36,000
I CAN ANSWER

1074
00:54:36,000 --> 00:54:38,000
FOR MR. AND MRS. GARDINER.

1075
00:54:38,000 --> 00:54:39,000
WE HAVE NO FIXED ENGAGEMENTS.

1076
00:54:39,000 --> 00:54:41,000
AND SHALL WE HEAR YOU PLAY?

1077
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:45,000
IF YOU INSIST UPON IT,
YES, YOU SHALL.

1078
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:47,000
( piano playing )

1079
00:54:47,000 --> 00:54:51,000
♪ SAY YE WHO BORROW ♪

1080
00:54:51,000 --> 00:54:55,000
♪ LOVE'S FLEETING SPELL ♪

1081
00:54:55,000 --> 00:55:00,000
♪ WHAT IS THIS SORROW ♪

1082
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:04,000
♪ NAUGHT CAN DISPEL? ♪

1083
00:55:04,000 --> 00:55:08,000
♪ WHAT IS THIS SORROW ♪

1084
00:55:08,000 --> 00:55:11,000
♪ NAUGHT CAN DISPEL? ♪

1085
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:16,000
♪ WHAT IS THIS SORROW ♪

1086
00:55:16,000 --> 00:55:21,000
♪ NAUGHT CAN DISPEL? ♪

1087
00:55:28,000 --> 00:55:33,000
ABSOLUTELY MARVELOUS.

1088
00:55:36,000 --> 00:55:37,000
WILL YOU NOT PLAY AGAIN?

1089
00:55:37,000 --> 00:55:39,000
YOU PLAYED THAT SONG
SO BEAUTIFULLY.

1090
00:55:39,000 --> 00:55:41,000
NOT VERY BEAUTIFULLY.

1091
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:42,000
NOT FAITHFULLY AT ALL.

1092
00:55:42,000 --> 00:55:45,000
YOU MUST HAVE SEEN HOW I
FUDGED AND SLURRED MY WAY

1093
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:47,000
THROUGH THE DIFFICULT PASSAGES.

1094
00:55:47,000 --> 00:55:50,000
IT IS
A BEAUTIFUL INSTRUMENT THOUGH.

1095
00:55:50,000 --> 00:55:52,000
MY BROTHER GAVE IT
TO ME THIS WEEK.

1096
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:53,000
HE IS SO GOOD.

1097
00:55:53,000 --> 00:55:55,000
I DON'T DESERVE IT.

1098
00:55:55,000 --> 00:55:57,000
I'M SURE YOU DO.

1099
00:55:57,000 --> 00:55:59,000
YOUR BROTHER THINKS YOU DO

1100
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:04,000
AND AS YOU KNOW,
HE IS NEVER WRONG.

1101
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:07,000
NOW, IT IS YOUR TURN.

1102
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:09,000
OH, I ABSOLUTELY INSIST.

1103
00:56:09,000 --> 00:56:11,000
IN FRONT OF ALL
THESE PEOPLE?

1104
00:56:11,000 --> 00:56:14,000
Georgiana:
I WILL PLAY,
BUT PLEASE

1105
00:56:14,000 --> 00:56:16,000
DON'T MAKE ME SING.

1106
00:56:16,000 --> 00:56:19,000
IF YOU LIKE.

1107
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:22,000
( playing Beethoven )

1108
00:56:22,000 --> 00:56:23,000
PRAY, MISS ELIZA

1109
00:56:23,000 --> 00:56:25,000
ARE THE MILITIA
STILL QUARTERED AT MERYTON?

1110
00:56:25,000 --> 00:56:27,000
NO, THEY
ARE ENCAMPED

1111
00:56:27,000 --> 00:56:28,000
AT BRIGHTON
FOR THE SUMMER.

1112
00:56:28,000 --> 00:56:31,000
THAT MUST BE A GREAT
LOSS FOR YOUR FAMILY.

1113
00:56:31,000 --> 00:56:35,000
WE ARE ENDURING IT
AS BEST WE CAN, MISS BINGLEY.

1114
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:38,000
I SHOULD HAVE THOUGHT
ONE GENTLEMAN'S ABSENCE

1115
00:56:38,000 --> 00:56:42,000
MIGHT HAVE CAUSED
PARTICULAR PANGS.

1116
00:56:42,000 --> 00:56:44,000
I CAN'T IMAGINE WHO YOU MEAN.

1117
00:56:44,000 --> 00:56:46,000
I UNDERSTOOD
THAT CERTAIN LADIES

1118
00:56:46,000 --> 00:56:49,000
FOUND THE SOCIETY
OF MR. WICKHAM

1119
00:56:49,000 --> 00:56:50,000
CURIOUSLY AGREEABLE.

1120
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:53,000
( music stops )

1121
00:56:53,000 --> 00:56:54,000
I'M SO SORRY...

1122
00:56:54,000 --> 00:56:55,000
I'M NEGLECTING YOU.

1123
00:56:55,000 --> 00:56:56,000
HOW CAN YOU PLAY

1124
00:56:56,000 --> 00:56:58,000
WITH NO ONE
TO TURN THE PAGES?

1125
00:56:58,000 --> 00:57:01,000
( music resumes )

1126
00:57:01,000 --> 00:57:06,000
THERE, ALLOW ME.

1127
00:57:51,000 --> 00:57:54,000
HOW VERY ILL ELIZA BENNET
LOOKED THIS EVENING.

1128
00:57:54,000 --> 00:57:55,000
I'VE NEVER
IN MY LIFE

1129
00:57:55,000 --> 00:57:57,000
SEEN ANYONE
SO MUCH ALTERED

1130
00:57:57,000 --> 00:57:59,000
AS SHE IS
SINCE THE WINTER.

1131
00:57:59,000 --> 00:58:00,000
QUITE SO, MY DEAR.

1132
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:02,000
SHE'S GROWN SO BROWN
AND COARSE.

1133
00:58:02,000 --> 00:58:04,000
LOUISA AND I
WERE AGREEING

1134
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:06,000
THAT WE SHOULD
HARDLY KNOW HER.

1135
00:58:06,000 --> 00:58:08,000
WHAT DO YOU SAY,
MR. DARCY?

1136
00:58:08,000 --> 00:58:09,000
I NOTICED
NO GREAT DIFFERENCE.

1137
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:12,000
SHE IS, I SUPPOSE,
A LITTLE TANNED.

1138
00:58:12,000 --> 00:58:14,000
HARDLY SURPRISING
WHEN ONE TRAVELS IN THE SUMMER.

1139
00:58:14,000 --> 00:58:17,000
MMM, FOR MY PART,
I MUST CONFESS

1140
00:58:17,000 --> 00:58:19,000
I NEVER SAW ANY
BEAUTY IN HER FACE.

1141
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:22,000
HER FEATURES ARE
NOT AT ALL HANDSOME.

1142
00:58:22,000 --> 00:58:23,000
HER COMPLEXION

1143
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:24,000
HAS NO BRILLIANCY.

1144
00:58:24,000 --> 00:58:27,000
OH, HER TEETH ARE TOLERABLE,
I SUPPOSE, BUT...

1145
00:58:27,000 --> 00:58:29,000
NOTHING OUT OF
THE COMMON WAY.

1146
00:58:29,000 --> 00:58:30,000
( chuckles )

1147
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:32,000
AND AS FOR HER EYES

1148
00:58:32,000 --> 00:58:35,000
WHICH I HAVE SOMETIMES
HEARD CALLED "FINE"

1149
00:58:35,000 --> 00:58:40,000
I COULD NEVER PERCEIVE
ANYTHING EXTRAORDINARY IN THEM.

1150
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:42,000
AND IN HER AIR ALTOGETHER

1151
00:58:42,000 --> 00:58:44,000
THERE'S A SELF-SUFFICIENCY
WITHOUT FASHION

1152
00:58:44,000 --> 00:58:46,000
WHICH I FIND INTOLERABLE.

1153
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:47,000
I THINK...

1154
00:58:47,000 --> 00:58:50,000
I REMEMBER
WHEN WE FIRST KNEW HER

1155
00:58:50,000 --> 00:58:51,000
IN HERTFORDSHIRE

1156
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:54,000
HOW AMAZED WE ALL WERE
TO FIND HER A REPUTED BEAUTY.

1157
00:58:54,000 --> 00:58:57,000
I PARTICULARLY RECALL YOU,
MR. DARCY

1158
00:58:57,000 --> 00:59:00,000
ONE NIGHT AFTER THEY'D
BEEN DINING AT NETHERFIELD

1159
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:01,000
SAYING, "SHE A BEAUTY?

1160
00:59:01,000 --> 00:59:04,000
I SHOULD AS SOON
CALL HER MOTHER A WIT."

1161
00:59:04,000 --> 00:59:06,000
( women laughing )

1162
00:59:06,000 --> 00:59:10,000
OH, BUT AFTERWARDS, SHE
SEEMED TO IMPROVE ON YOU.

1163
00:59:10,000 --> 00:59:14,000
I EVEN BELIEVE YOU THOUGHT HER
RATHER PRETTY AT ONE TIME.

1164
00:59:14,000 --> 00:59:16,000
YES, I DID.

1165
00:59:16,000 --> 00:59:18,000
THAT WAS ONLY WHEN
I FIRST KNEW HER.

1166
00:59:18,000 --> 00:59:20,000
FOR IT HAS BEEN
MANY MONTHS NOW

1167
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:21,000
SINCE I HAVE CONSIDERED HER

1168
00:59:21,000 --> 00:59:26,000
ONE OF THE HANDSOMEST WOMEN
OF MY ACQUAINTANCE.

1169
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:17,000
( birds singing )

1170
01:00:20,000 --> 01:00:23,000
NO, NO,
THE GREEN ONE.

1171
01:00:23,000 --> 01:00:27,000
YES, THAT WILL DO.

1172
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:29,000
( mumbling ):
GOOD.

1173
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:30,000
NEVER MIND.

1174
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:31,000
( clears throat )

1175
01:00:31,000 --> 01:00:36,000
( birds singing )

1176
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:53,000
IF YOU PLEASE, MA'AM.

1177
01:00:53,000 --> 01:00:55,000
THE POST'S JUST COME.
THANK YOU, HANNAH.
A GOOD GIRL,
THAT.
VERY
OBLIGING.
TWO LETTERS FROM JANE.
AT LAST! I'D BEEN WONDERING
WHY WE HADN'T...
THIS ONE WAS MISDIRECTED
AT FIRST.
NO WONDER, FOR SHE WROTE
THE DIRECTION VERY ILL INDEED.
WOULD YOU BE VERY ANGRY
IF I BEG YOU
TO POSTPONE OUR OUTING?
NOT AT ALL.
OF COURSE YOU WANT
TO READ YOUR LETTERS.
YOUR UNCLE AND I
WILL WALK TO THE CHURCH
AND CALL BACK
IN AN HOUR.
THANK YOU. YOU'RE VERY KIND.
Jane:
"MY DEAREST LIZZY:
"I HOPE YOUR JOURNEY HAS BEEN AS
DELIGHTFUL AS YOU ANTICIPATED.
"WE ALL MISS YOU
"OUR FATHER MOST OF ALL,
I BELIEVE.
"I CONFESS I'VE HARDLY HAD TIME
TO WRITE.
"MY NEPHEWS AND NIECES
HAVE COMMANDEERED EVERY MOMENT
"BUT THEY ARE
SUCH DEAR CHILDREN.
"OUR MOTHER INDEED
FINDS THEIR EXUBERANCE
A LITTLE TRYING FOR HER NERVES."
OH... MAMMA.
"SHE SPENDS MUCH OF THE DAY
ABOVE STAIRS IN HER ROOM
"OR WITH MRS. PHILLIPS.
"OH, DEAREST LIZZY,
SINCE WRITING THE ABOVE
"SOMETHING HAS OCCURRED
"OF A MOST UNEXPECTED
AND SERIOUS NATURE.
"BUT I'M AFRAID OF ALARMING YOU.
"BE ASSURED WE ARE ALL WELL.
WHAT I HAVE TO SAY
RELATES TO POOR LYDIA."
LYDIA!
Jane:
"AN EXPRESS CAME AT 12:00
LAST NIGHT
JUST AS WE WERE ALL
GONE TO BED."
( pounding on door )
Mrs. Bennet:
OH, MR. BENNET, WHAT IS IT?
ARE WE TO BE MURDERED
IN OUR BEDS?
Jane:
"THE LETTER
WAS FROM COLONEL FORSTER
"TO INFORM US THAT LYDIA
WAS GONE OFF TO SCOTLAND
"WITH ONE OF HIS OFFICERS.
TO OWN THE TRUTH, WITH WICKHAM."
OH! OH, LYDIA!
OH, MR. BENNET,
WE ARE ALL RUINED.
Jane:
"YOU WILL IMAGINE
OUR SURPRISE AND SHOCK.
"TO KITTY, HOWEVER
IT DOES NOT SEEM
SO WHOLLY UNEXPECTED."
( loud sobbing )
"I AM VERY, VERY SORRY.
"SO IMPRUDENT A MATCH
ON BOTH SIDES.
"BUT I AM WILLING
TO HOPE THE BEST
AND THAT HIS CHARACTER
HAS BEEN MISUNDERSTOOD."
I WISH I COULD BELIEVE IT.
"HIS CHOICE IS DISINTERESTED,
AT LEAST.
HE MUST KNOW THAT OUR FATHER
CAN GIVE HIM NOTHING."
YES, THAT IS TRUE.
BUT HOW COULD HE DO THIS?
SHE IS SILLY ENOUGH
FOR ANYTHING.
BUT WICKHAM LOVE LYDIA?
MARRY LYDIA?
THERE IS ONE LADY I SHALL BE
VERY LOATH TO PART FROM.
Jane:
"WE EXPECT THEM SOON
"RETURNED FROM GRETNA,
MAN AND WIFE.
"BUT I MUST CONCLUDE
"I CANNOT BE AWAY
FROM OUR POOR MOTHER LONG.
"I SHALL WRITE AGAIN
AS SOON AS I HAVE NEWS."
"MY DEAREST LIZZY:
"I HARDLY KNOW WHAT TO WRITE
BUT I HAVE BAD NEWS.
"IMPRUDENT
AS A MARRIAGE WOULD BE
"WE NOW FEAR WORSE--
THAT IT HAS NOT TAKEN PLACE.
THAT WICKHAM NEVER INTENDED
TO MARRY LYDIA AT ALL."
GREAT GOD! I KNEW IT.
"I CANNOT THINK SO ILL OF HIM."
I CAN.
AND POOR LYDIA.
POOR, STUPID GIRL.
"COLONEL FORSTER SAID HE FEARED
THAT WICKHAM WAS NOT A MAN
TO BE TRUSTED."
Darcy:
"SHE WAS THEN BUT 15 YEARS OLD."
Jane:
"THEY WERE TRACED
AS FAR AS CLAPHAM
"AND TO LONDON OUR FATHER
HAS GONE WITH COLONEL FORSTER
"TO TRY TO DISCOVER THEM.
"I CANNOT HELP BUT BEG YOU ALL
TO COME HERE AS SOON
AS POSSIBLE."
OH, YES.
WHERE IS MY UNCLE?
IF YOU PLEASE,
MA'AM.
MISS BENNET,
I HOPE THIS IS...
I BEG YOUR PARDON.
I MUST FIND MR. GARDINER
ON BUSINESS
THAT CANNOT BE DELAYED.
I HAVE NOT AN INSTANT
TO LOSE.
GOOD GOD, WHAT IS THE MATTER?
OF COURSE, I WILL NOT DETAIN YOU
FOR A MOMENT
BUT LET ME GO
OR LET THE SERVANT GO
AND FETCH MR. AND MRS. GARDINER.
YOU CANNOT GO
YOURSELF.
NO, I MUST.
COME, THIS WILL BE
FOR THE BEST.
HELLO THERE!
WOULD YOU HAVE MR.
AND MRS. GARDINER
FETCHED AT ONCE.
THEY WALKED
IN THE DIRECTION OF...
THE CHURCH.
YES, SIR, AT ONCE.
YOU ARE NOT WELL.
MAY I NOT CALL A DOCTOR?
NO. I AM WELL.
I AM WELL.
IS THERE NOTHING
YOU CAN TAKE
FOR YOUR PRESENT RELIEF?
A GLASS OF WINE?
CAN I GET YOU ONE?
TRULY YOU LOOK VERY ILL.
NO, I THANK YOU.
THERE IS NOTHING
THE MATTER WITH ME.
I AM QUITE WELL.
I AM ONLY DISTRESSED
BY SOME DREADFUL NEWS
WHICH I'VE JUST RECEIVED.
I'M SORRY.
FORGIVE ME.
OH, NO.
I'VE JUST RECEIVED
A LETTER FROM JANE
WITH SUCH DREADFUL NEWS.
IT CANNOT BE CONCEALED
FROM ANYONE.
MY YOUNGEST SISTER
HAS LEFT ALL HER FRIENDS.
HAS ELOPED.
HAS THROWN HERSELF
INTO THE POWER
OF MR. WICKHAM.
THEY HAVE RUN AWAY
TOGETHER FROM BRIGHTON.
YOU KNOW HIM TOO WELL
TO DOUBT THE REST.
SHE HAS NO MONEY,
NO CONNECTIONS.
NOTHING THAT CAN
TEMPT HIM.
WHEN I THINK THAT I
MIGHT HAVE PREVENTED IT.
I, WHO KNEW WHAT HE WAS.
HAD HIS CHARACTER BEEN KNOWN,
THIS COULD NOT HAVE HAPPENED.
BUT IT IS ALL
TOO LATE NOW.
I AM GRIEVED INDEED.
GRIEVED, SHOCKED.
BUT IS IT CERTAIN,
ABSOLUTELY CERTAIN?
OH, YES.
THEY LEFT BRIGHTON TOGETHER
ON SUNDAY NIGHT.
THEY WERE TRACED
AS FAR AS LONDON
BUT NOT BEYOND.
THEY ARE CERTAINLY
NOT GONE TO SCOTLAND.
AND WHAT HAS BEEN DONE?
WHAT HAS BEEN ATTEMPTED
TO RECOVER HER?
MY FATHER HAS GONE
TO LONDON
AND JANE WRITES
TO BEG MY UNCLE'S
IMMEDIATE ASSISTANCE.
I HOPE THAT WE SHALL LEAVE
WITHIN HALF AN HOUR.
BUT WHAT CAN BE DONE?
I KNOW VERY WELL
THAT NOTHING CAN BE DONE.
HOW IS SUCH A MAN
TO BE WORKED ON?
HOW ARE THEY EVEN
TO BE DISCOVERED?
I HAVE NOT THE SMALLEST HOPE.
SHE IS LOST FOREVER
AND OUR WHOLE FAMILY
MUST PARTAKE
OF HER RUIN AND DISGRACE.
I'M AFRAID YOU HAVE LONG
BEEN DESIRING MY ABSENCE.
THIS UNFORTUNATE AFFAIR
WILL, I FEAR
PREVENT MY SISTER'S
HAVING THE PLEASURE
OF SEEING YOU
AT PEMBERLEY TODAY.
OH, YES.
BE SO KIND AS TO APOLOGIZE
FOR US TO MISS DARCY.
SAY THAT URGENT BUSINESS
CALLS US HOME
IMMEDIATELY.
AND IF YOU WOULD BE
SO KIND
AS TO CONCEAL
THE UNHAPPY TRUTH
AS LONG AS POSSIBLE.
I KNOW THAT IT CANNOT BE LONG.
YOU MAY BE ASSURED
OF MY SECRECY.
BUT I HAVE STAYED TOO LONG.
I SHALL LEAVE YOU NOW.
YES. THANK YOU.
GOOD-BYE.
I SHALL NEVER SEE HIM AGAIN.
EVEN IF WHAT YOU SAY
OF WICKHAM IS TRUE
I STILL CANNOT BELIEVE
THIS OF LYDIA.
EVER SINCE THE MILITIA
WERE QUARTERED AT MERYTON
THERE HAS BEEN NOTHING
BUT LOVE, FLIRTATION
AND OFFICERS IN HER HEAD!
YOU MUST NOT ASSUME
THE WORST.
IT MAY YET BE
THAT THIS IS ALL
A MISUNDERSTANDING
OR JUST A PASSING FOLLY
THAT HER FRIENDS
CAN HUSH UP
AND WILL IN TIME
BE QUITE FORGOTTEN.
IT IS POSSIBLE, LIZZY.
INDEED, IT IS.
WHY WOULD ANY YOUNG MAN
FORM A DESIGN AGAINST A GIRL
WHO'S BY NO MEANS
UNPROTECTED OR FRIENDLESS?
AND WHO'S ACTUALLY STAYING
IN THE COLONEL'S FAMILY?
LOOK AT IT ANY WAY YOU LIKE--
THE TEMPTATION IS
NOT WORTH THE RISK.
NOT, PERHAPS, A RISK
IN HIS OWN INTEREST
BUT I DO BELIEVE HIM CAPABLE
OF RISKING EVERYTHING ELSE.
( piano playing )
YOU ARE VERY QUIET
THIS EVENING, MR. DARCY.
I SINCERELY HOPE
YOU'RE NOT PINING
FOR THE LOSS
OF MISS ELIZA BENNET.

1178
01:00:55,000 --> 01:00:57,000
WHAT?

1179
01:00:57,000 --> 01:00:58,000
EXCUSE ME.

1180
01:00:58,000 --> 01:01:03,000
( clears throat )

1181
01:01:06,000 --> 01:01:11,000
( children talking
and laughing )

1182
01:01:28,000 --> 01:01:33,000
( children greeting Eliza )

1183
01:01:35,000 --> 01:01:37,000
OH, LIZZY.

1184
01:01:37,000 --> 01:01:39,000
I AM SO GLAD TO SEE YOU.

1185
01:01:39,000 --> 01:01:40,000
HAS ANYTHING BEEN HEARD?

1186
01:01:40,000 --> 01:01:42,000
NO, BUT NOW OUR
UNCLE IS COME

1187
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:44,000
I HOPE EVERYTHING
WILL BE WELL.

1188
01:01:44,000 --> 01:01:46,000
OUR FATHER LEFT
FOR TOWN ON TUESDAY.

1189
01:01:46,000 --> 01:01:47,000
WE'VE HEARD
FROM HIM ONCE

1190
01:01:47,000 --> 01:01:49,000
TO SAY HE HAS
ARRIVED IN SAFETY.

1191
01:01:49,000 --> 01:01:51,000
MAMMA HAS BEEN ASKING
FOR YOU SINCE DAYBREAK.

1192
01:01:51,000 --> 01:01:53,000
HOW IS SHE?

1193
01:01:53,000 --> 01:01:56,000
SHE HAS NOT YET
LEFT HER ROOM.

1194
01:01:56,000 --> 01:01:58,000
AND YOU LOOK PALE.

1195
01:01:58,000 --> 01:02:01,000
OH, JANE, HOW MUCH
YOU MUST HAVE GONE THROUGH.

1196
01:02:01,000 --> 01:02:03,000
I AM SO HAPPY
TO SEE YOU, LIZZY.

1197
01:02:03,000 --> 01:02:08,000
COME.

1198
01:02:08,000 --> 01:02:10,000
OH!

1199
01:02:10,000 --> 01:02:12,000
OH, LIZZY.

1200
01:02:12,000 --> 01:02:14,000
OH, BROTHER...

1201
01:02:14,000 --> 01:02:18,000
WE ARE ALL RUINED FOREVER.

1202
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:21,000
IF ONLY MR. BENNET HAD
TAKEN US ALL TO BRIGHTON

1203
01:02:21,000 --> 01:02:23,000
NONE OF THIS WOULD
HAVE HAPPENED.

1204
01:02:23,000 --> 01:02:25,000
I BLAME THOSE FORSTERS.

1205
01:02:25,000 --> 01:02:27,000
I AM SURE THERE WAS
SOME GREAT NEGLECT

1206
01:02:27,000 --> 01:02:31,000
ON THEIR PART, FOR SHE
IS NOT THE KIND OF GIRL

1207
01:02:31,000 --> 01:02:33,000
TO DO THAT
SORT OF THING

1208
01:02:33,000 --> 01:02:36,000
IF SHE HAD BEEN
PROPERLY LOOKED AFTER.

1209
01:02:36,000 --> 01:02:37,000
MAMMA.

1210
01:02:37,000 --> 01:02:39,000
NOW HERE IS MR. BENNET
GONE AWAY.

1211
01:02:39,000 --> 01:02:42,000
I KNOW HE WILL FIGHT WICKHAM,
AND THEN HE WILL BE KILLED

1212
01:02:42,000 --> 01:02:44,000
AND THEN WHAT IS TO BECOME
OF US ALL?

1213
01:02:44,000 --> 01:02:47,000
THOSE COLLINSES
WILL TURN US OUT

1214
01:02:47,000 --> 01:02:50,000
BEFORE HE IS COLD
IN HIS GRAVE

1215
01:02:50,000 --> 01:02:53,000
AND IF YOU ARE NOT
KIND TO US, BROTHER

1216
01:02:53,000 --> 01:02:55,000
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT WE SHALL DO.

1217
01:02:55,000 --> 01:02:57,000
SISTER, CALM DOWN.

1218
01:02:57,000 --> 01:02:59,000
NOTHING DREADFUL
WILL HAPPEN.

1219
01:02:59,000 --> 01:03:01,000
I SHALL BE IN LONDON
TOMORROW MORNING.

1220
01:03:01,000 --> 01:03:04,000
THERE WE WILL CONSULT
AS TO WHAT IS TO BE DONE.

1221
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:05,000
YES! YOU MUST

1222
01:03:05,000 --> 01:03:08,000
FIND THEM OUT, AND IF
THEY BE NOT MARRIED

1223
01:03:08,000 --> 01:03:10,000
YOU MUST MAKE THEM MARRY

1224
01:03:10,000 --> 01:03:13,000
BUT ABOVE ALL,
KEEP MR. BENNET FROM FIGHTING.

1225
01:03:13,000 --> 01:03:15,000
I'M SURE HE DOES NOT
MEAN TO FIGHT.

1226
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:17,000
OH, YES! YES, HE DOES

1227
01:03:17,000 --> 01:03:19,000
AND WICKHAM WILL KILL HIM SURE

1228
01:03:19,000 --> 01:03:21,000
UNLESS YOU CAN PREVENT IT,
BROTHER.

1229
01:03:21,000 --> 01:03:25,000
YOU MUST TELL HIM WHAT
A DREADFUL STATE I'M IN.

1230
01:03:25,000 --> 01:03:30,000
AND HOW I HAVE SUCH TREMBLINGS
AND FLUTTERINGS ALL OVER ME.

1231
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:33,000
SUCH SPASMS IN MY SIDE
AND PAINS IN MY HEAD

1232
01:03:33,000 --> 01:03:37,000
AND BEATINGS AT MY HEART
THAT I CAN GET NO REST

1233
01:03:37,000 --> 01:03:38,000
EITHER NIGHT OR DAY.

1234
01:03:38,000 --> 01:03:39,000
SISTER, CALM YOURSELF.

1235
01:03:39,000 --> 01:03:41,000
TELL LYDIA NOT TO
GIVE ANY DIRECTIONS

1236
01:03:41,000 --> 01:03:45,000
ABOUT WEDDING CLOTHES
TILL SHE HAS SEEN ME.

1237
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:47,000
FOR SHE DOES NOT KNOW

1238
01:03:47,000 --> 01:03:49,000
WHICH ARE THE BEST WAREHOUSES.

1239
01:03:49,000 --> 01:03:54,000
( sobbing )

1240
01:04:16,000 --> 01:04:18,000
THIS IS THE MOST
UNFORTUNATE AFFAIR

1241
01:04:18,000 --> 01:04:21,000
AND WILL PROBABLY
BE MUCH TALKED OF.

1242
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:23,000
YES. THANK YOU, MARY.

1243
01:04:23,000 --> 01:04:25,000
I THINK WE HAVE ALL
APPREHENDED THAT MUCH.

1244
01:04:25,000 --> 01:04:28,000
BUT WE MUST STEM
THE TIDE OF MALICE

1245
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:31,000
AND POUR INTO EACH OTHER'S
WOUNDED BOSOMS THE BALM

1246
01:04:31,000 --> 01:04:33,000
OF SISTERLY
CONSOLATION.

1247
01:04:33,000 --> 01:04:36,000
MARY, PASS THE POTATOES
TO YOUR AUNT GARDINER.

1248
01:04:36,000 --> 01:04:37,000
I BEG YOUR PARDON.

1249
01:04:37,000 --> 01:04:38,000
OH, NEVER MIND...

1250
01:04:38,000 --> 01:04:39,000
I WILL.

1251
01:04:39,000 --> 01:04:41,000
THANK YOU, KITTY.

1252
01:04:41,000 --> 01:04:43,000
THAT'S THE FIRST KIND WORD

1253
01:04:43,000 --> 01:04:46,000
I'VE HAD FROM ANYONE
SINCE LYDIA WENT AWAY.

1254
01:04:46,000 --> 01:04:48,000
IT IS MOST UNFAIR
FOR IT IS NOT AS IF

1255
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:49,000
I HAVE DONE
ANYTHING NAUGHTY

1256
01:04:49,000 --> 01:04:52,000
AND I DON'T SEE THAT
LYDIA HAS DONE ANYTHING

1257
01:04:52,000 --> 01:04:53,000
SO VERY DREADFUL EITHER.

1258
01:04:53,000 --> 01:04:54,000
KITTY, PLEASE.

1259
01:04:54,000 --> 01:04:56,000
UNHAPPY AS THE
EVENT MUST BE

1260
01:04:56,000 --> 01:04:59,000
FOR LYDIA, WE
MUST DRAW FROM IT

1261
01:04:59,000 --> 01:05:00,000
THIS USEFUL LESSON--

1262
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:02,000
THAT LOSS OF VIRTUE
IN A FEMALE

1263
01:05:02,000 --> 01:05:04,000
IS IRRETRIEVABLE.

1264
01:05:04,000 --> 01:05:06,000
MY DEAR MARY, THIS
IS HARDLY HELPFUL.

1265
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:08,000
FOR A WOMAN'S REPUTATION

1266
01:05:08,000 --> 01:05:10,000
IS NO LESS BRITTLE
THAN IT IS BEAUTIFUL

1267
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:12,000
AND THEREFORE WE
CANNOT BE TOO GUARDED

1268
01:05:12,000 --> 01:05:14,000
IN OUR BEHAVIOR

1269
01:05:14,000 --> 01:05:17,000
TOWARDS THE UNDESERVING
OF THE OTHER SEX.

1270
01:05:17,000 --> 01:05:22,000
YES. THANK YOU, MARY.

1271
01:05:25,000 --> 01:05:30,000
( door opening )

1272
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:39,000
NOW, JANE, TELL ME
EVERYTHING ABOUT IT

1273
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:41,000
THAT I'VE NOT ALREADY HEARD.

1274
01:05:41,000 --> 01:05:44,000
WHAT DID COLONEL
FORSTER SAY?

1275
01:05:44,000 --> 01:05:47,000
HAD THEY NO APPREHENSION
ABOUT ANYTHING

1276
01:05:47,000 --> 01:05:49,000
BEFORE THE ELOPEMENT
TOOK PLACE?

1277
01:05:49,000 --> 01:05:52,000
COLONEL FORSTER
DID OWN HE SUSPECTED

1278
01:05:52,000 --> 01:05:54,000
SOME PARTIALITY
ON LYDIA'S SIDE

1279
01:05:54,000 --> 01:05:57,000
BUT NOTHING TO
GIVE HIM ANY ALARM.

1280
01:05:57,000 --> 01:05:59,000
LIZZY...

1281
01:05:59,000 --> 01:06:00,000
I FEEL I AM TO BLAME

1282
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:02,000
FOR IT WAS I WHO URGED YOU

1283
01:06:02,000 --> 01:06:04,000
NOT TO MAKE WICKHAM'S
BAD CONDUCT KNOWN

1284
01:06:04,000 --> 01:06:07,000
AND NOW POOR LYDIA
IS SUFFERING FOR IT.

1285
01:06:07,000 --> 01:06:09,000
NO ONE ELSE SUSPECTED
HIM FOR A MOMENT.

1286
01:06:09,000 --> 01:06:11,000
I AM, I AM TO BLAME.

1287
01:06:11,000 --> 01:06:13,000
YOU ARE NOT TO BLAME.

1288
01:06:13,000 --> 01:06:15,000
NO MORE THAN I
OR MR. DARCY

1289
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:19,000
OR ANYONE ELSE
DECEIVED BY WICKHAM.

1290
01:06:19,000 --> 01:06:21,000
YOU HAVE NOTHING
TO BLAME YOURSELF FOR.

1291
01:06:21,000 --> 01:06:26,000
OTHERS ARE CULPABLE,
NOT YOU.

1292
01:06:26,000 --> 01:06:28,000
SHE WROTE A NOTE
FOR MRS. FORSTER

1293
01:06:28,000 --> 01:06:33,000
BEFORE SHE WENT AWAY.

1294
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:36,000
"MY DEAR HARRIET

1295
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:40,000
"YOU WILL LAUGH WHEN
YOU KNOW WHERE I AM GONE

1296
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:42,000
"AND I CANNOT HELP
LAUGHING MYSELF

1297
01:06:42,000 --> 01:06:44,000
"AT YOUR SURPRISE
TOMORROW MORNING

1298
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:46,000
AS SOON AS I AM MISSED."

1299
01:06:46,000 --> 01:06:48,000
Lydia:
"I AM GOING TO GRETNA GREEN

1300
01:06:48,000 --> 01:06:50,000
"AND IF YOU CANNOT
GUESS WITH WHOM

1301
01:06:50,000 --> 01:06:51,000
"I SHALL THINK YOU A SIMPLETON

1302
01:06:51,000 --> 01:06:54,000
"FOR THERE IS BUT ONE MAN
IN THE WORLD I LOVE.

1303
01:06:54,000 --> 01:06:56,000
"DON'T SEND THEM WORD
AT LONGBOURN

1304
01:06:56,000 --> 01:06:58,000
"OF MY GOING.

1305
01:06:58,000 --> 01:07:00,000
"IT WILL MAKE THE SURPRISE
ALL THE GREATER

1306
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:04,000
"WHEN I WRITE TO THEM AND SIGN
MY NAME LYDIA WICKHAM.

1307
01:07:04,000 --> 01:07:05,000
"WHAT A GOOD JOKE IT WILL BE.

1308
01:07:05,000 --> 01:07:07,000
I CAN SCARCELY WRITE
FOR LAUGHING."

1309
01:07:07,000 --> 01:07:11,000
( giggling )

1310
01:07:11,000 --> 01:07:13,000
THOUGHTLESS, THOUGHTLESS LYDIA.

1311
01:07:13,000 --> 01:07:15,000
WHAT A LETTER TO HAVE WRITTEN

1312
01:07:15,000 --> 01:07:16,000
AT SUCH A MOMENT.

1313
01:07:16,000 --> 01:07:18,000
AT LEAST IT SHOWS
SHE BELIEVED

1314
01:07:18,000 --> 01:07:19,000
WICKHAM'S PURPOSE
WAS MARRIAGE

1315
01:07:19,000 --> 01:07:22,000
WHATEVER HE MIGHT HAVE
PERSUADED HER TO AFTERWARDS.

1316
01:07:22,000 --> 01:07:23,000
OUR POOR FATHER.

1317
01:07:23,000 --> 01:07:27,000
HOW HE MUST HAVE FELT IT.

1318
01:07:27,000 --> 01:07:29,000
I NEVER SAW
ANYONE SO SHOCKED.

1319
01:07:29,000 --> 01:07:32,000
HE COULD NOT SPEAK A WORD
FOR FULLY TEN MINUTES.

1320
01:07:32,000 --> 01:07:35,000
OUR MOTHER WAS TAKEN ILL
WITH THE HYSTERICS

1321
01:07:35,000 --> 01:07:38,000
AND THE WHOLE HOUSE
WAS IN CONFUSION.

1322
01:07:38,000 --> 01:07:41,000
LADY LUCAS HAS BEEN VERY KIND,
OFFERING HER SERVICES.

1323
01:07:41,000 --> 01:07:43,000
SHE HAD BETTER
HAD STAYED HOME.

1324
01:07:43,000 --> 01:07:44,000
ASSISTANCE IS IMPOSSIBLE

1325
01:07:44,000 --> 01:07:46,000
AND CONDOLENCE INSUFFERABLE.

1326
01:07:46,000 --> 01:07:50,000
LET HER TRIUMPH OVER US
AT A DISTANCE AND BE SATISFIED.

1327
01:07:50,000 --> 01:07:53,000
LIZZY, THAT IS UNKIND.

1328
01:07:53,000 --> 01:07:55,000
I'M SURE SHE MEANT WELL.

1329
01:07:55,000 --> 01:07:59,000
YES, PERHAPS SHE DID.

1330
01:07:59,000 --> 01:08:01,000
I AM SORRY.

1331
01:08:01,000 --> 01:08:05,000
IT'S JUST THAT I CAN'T HELP
BUT BE...

1332
01:08:05,000 --> 01:08:07,000
OH, JANE.

1333
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:09,000
JANE, DO YOU NOT SEE

1334
01:08:09,000 --> 01:08:12,000
THAT MORE THINGS HAVE BEEN
RUINED BY THIS BUSINESS

1335
01:08:12,000 --> 01:08:17,000
THAN LYDIA'S REPUTATION?

1336
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:38,000
Darcy:
I HAVE STAYED TOO LONG.

1337
01:08:38,000 --> 01:08:43,000
I SHALL LEAVE YOU NOW.

1338
01:08:44,000 --> 01:08:47,000
( soft knocking )

1339
01:08:47,000 --> 01:08:51,000
COME IN.

1340
01:08:51,000 --> 01:08:56,000
I THOUGHT YOU WOULD
NOT BE IN BED YET.

1341
01:09:03,000 --> 01:09:07,000
I'VE BEEN THINKING
ABOUT WHAT YOU SAID
THIS AFTERNOON.

1342
01:09:07,000 --> 01:09:09,000
THAT IT IS NOT ONLY
LYDIA'S REPUTATION

1343
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:11,000
THAT HAS BEEN RUINED.

1344
01:09:11,000 --> 01:09:13,000
I WAS ANGRY AND UPSET.

1345
01:09:13,000 --> 01:09:15,000
I SHOULD NOT
HAVE SAID IT.

1346
01:09:15,000 --> 01:09:17,000
IT DOES NO GOOD
TO DWELL ON IT.

1347
01:09:17,000 --> 01:09:20,000
YOU MEANT, I SUPPOSE,
THAT YOU AND I

1348
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:22,000
AND MARY AND KITTY

1349
01:09:22,000 --> 01:09:26,000
HAVE BEEN TAINTED
BY ASSOCIATION;

1350
01:09:26,000 --> 01:09:28,000
THAT OUR CHANCES OF
MAKING A GOOD MARRIAGE

1351
01:09:28,000 --> 01:09:33,000
HAVE BEEN MATERIALLY
DAMAGED BY LYDIA'S DISGRACE.

1352
01:09:34,000 --> 01:09:37,000
THE CHANCES OF ANY OF US
MAKING A GOOD MARRIAGE

1353
01:09:37,000 --> 01:09:39,000
WERE NEVER VERY GREAT

1354
01:09:39,000 --> 01:09:41,000
AND NOW I SHOULD SAY

1355
01:09:41,000 --> 01:09:43,000
THEY ARE NONEXISTENT.

1356
01:09:43,000 --> 01:09:46,000
NO ONE WILL SOLICIT
OUR SOCIETY AFTER THIS.

1357
01:09:46,000 --> 01:09:48,000
MR. DARCY MADE THAT
VERY CLEAR TO ME.

1358
01:09:48,000 --> 01:09:50,000
MR. DARCY?

1359
01:09:50,000 --> 01:09:54,000
DOES HE KNOW OUR TROUBLES?

1360
01:09:54,000 --> 01:09:59,000
HE HAPPENED UPON ME A MOMENT
AFTER I FIRST READ YOUR LETTER.

1361
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:03,000
HE WAS VERY KIND,
VERY GENTLEMAN-LIKE

1362
01:10:03,000 --> 01:10:05,000
BUT HE MADE IT VERY CLEAR

1363
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:10,000
HE WANTED NOTHING MORE
THAN TO BE OUT OF MY SIGHT.

1364
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:16,000
HE WILL NOT BE RENEWING
HIS ADDRESSES TO ME.

1365
01:10:16,000 --> 01:10:17,000
HE WILL MAKE VERY SURE

1366
01:10:17,000 --> 01:10:21,000
HIS FRIEND DOES NOT
RENEW HIS TO YOU.

1367
01:10:21,000 --> 01:10:22,000
I NEVER EXPECTED
MR. BINGLEY

1368
01:10:22,000 --> 01:10:24,000
WOULD RENEW
HIS ADDRESSES, LIZZY.

1369
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:26,000
I AM QUITE RECONCILED
TO THAT.

1370
01:10:26,000 --> 01:10:31,000
SURELY YOU DO NOT DESIRE
MR. DARCY'S ATTENTIONS, DO YOU?

1371
01:10:32,000 --> 01:10:34,000
NO. NO. I NEVER SOUGHT THEM.

1372
01:10:34,000 --> 01:10:38,000
BUT YOU DO THINK HE WAS
INTENDING TO RENEW THEM?

1373
01:10:38,000 --> 01:10:39,000
YOU THINK HE IS

1374
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:41,000
STILL IN LOVE WITH YOU?

1375
01:10:41,000 --> 01:10:43,000
I DON'T KNOW.

1376
01:10:43,000 --> 01:10:46,000
I DON'T KNOW WHAT
HE WAS TWO DAYS AGO.

1377
01:10:46,000 --> 01:10:48,000
ALL I KNOW IS THAT NOW, HE...

1378
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:50,000
OR ANY OTHER RESPECTABLE MAN

1379
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:55,000
WILL WANT NOTHING TO DO
WITH ANY OF US.

1380
01:10:59,000 --> 01:11:02,000
( horse braying )

1381
01:11:02,000 --> 01:11:04,000
Man:
GET SOME ALE FOR THAT GENTLEMAN.

1382
01:11:04,000 --> 01:11:09,000
COME ON, HURRY UP.

1383
01:11:14,000 --> 01:11:15,000
OH, LORD.

1384
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:17,000
LOOK WHO'S COMING.

1385
01:11:17,000 --> 01:11:18,000
WHO IS IT, KITTY?

1386
01:11:18,000 --> 01:11:20,000
MR. COLLINS, OF COURSE.

1387
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:25,000
WELL, I'M NOT GOING
TO SIT WITH HIM FOR ANYONE.

1388
01:11:34,000 --> 01:11:36,000
I HAD HOPED TO CONDOLE

1389
01:11:36,000 --> 01:11:38,000
WITH YOUR POOR FATHER
AND YOUR MOTHER.

1390
01:11:38,000 --> 01:11:40,000
OUR FATHER IS STILL
IN LONDON, SIR

1391
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:43,000
AND OUR MOTHER
IS NOT YET WELL ENOUGH

1392
01:11:43,000 --> 01:11:44,000
TO LEAVE HER ROOM.

1393
01:11:44,000 --> 01:11:46,000
AH... AH.

1394
01:11:46,000 --> 01:11:48,000
( clears throat )

1395
01:11:48,000 --> 01:11:50,000
I FEEL MYSELF CALLED ON

1396
01:11:50,000 --> 01:11:53,000
NOT ONLY BY OUR RELATIONSHIP

1397
01:11:53,000 --> 01:11:55,000
BUT MY SITUATION AS A CLERGYMAN

1398
01:11:55,000 --> 01:11:57,000
TO CONDOLE WITH YOU ALL

1399
01:11:57,000 --> 01:12:00,000
ON THE GRIEVOUS AFFLICTION
YOU ARE NOW SUFFERING UNDER.

1400
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:02,000
THANK YOU, SIR.

1401
01:12:02,000 --> 01:12:03,000
IT HAS OFTEN
BEEN SAID

1402
01:12:03,000 --> 01:12:06,000
THAT A FRIEND IN NEED
IS A FRIEND INDEED

1403
01:12:06,000 --> 01:12:08,000
SIR.

1404
01:12:08,000 --> 01:12:10,000
YES.

1405
01:12:10,000 --> 01:12:12,000
BE ASSURED, LADIES

1406
01:12:12,000 --> 01:12:15,000
THAT MRS. COLLINS AND MYSELF
SINCERELY SYMPATHIZE WITH YOU

1407
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:17,000
IN YOUR PRESENT DISTRESS

1408
01:12:17,000 --> 01:12:20,000
WHICH MUST BE
OF THE BITTEREST KIND

1409
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:23,000
PROCEEDING FROM A CAUSE
WHICH NO TIME CAN REMOVE.

1410
01:12:23,000 --> 01:12:26,000
THE DEATH OF YOUR SISTER

1411
01:12:26,000 --> 01:12:28,000
WOULD HAVE BEEN
A BLESSING IN COMPARISON.

1412
01:12:28,000 --> 01:12:30,000
IT IS MORE
TO BE LAMENTED

1413
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:32,000
BECAUSE THERE IS
REASON TO SUPPOSE

1414
01:12:32,000 --> 01:12:35,000
MY DEAR CHARLOTTE INFORMS ME

1415
01:12:35,000 --> 01:12:38,000
THAT THIS LICENTIOUSNESS
OF BEHAVIOR IN YOUR SISTER

1416
01:12:38,000 --> 01:12:41,000
HAS PROCEEDED FROM
A FAULTY DEGREE OF INDULGENCE

1417
01:12:41,000 --> 01:12:44,000
THOUGH I AM INCLINED
TO THINK THAT HER DISPOSITION

1418
01:12:44,000 --> 01:12:46,000
MUST BE NATURALLY BAD.

1419
01:12:46,000 --> 01:12:48,000
NOW, HOWSOEVER THAT MAY BE

1420
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:53,000
YOU ARE GRIEVOUSLY TO BE PITIED.

1421
01:12:54,000 --> 01:12:57,000
WE ARE VERY GRATEFUL,
SIR, FOR YOUR...

1422
01:12:57,000 --> 01:12:59,000
IN WHICH OPINION I AM JOINED

1423
01:12:59,000 --> 01:13:01,000
BY LADY CATHERINE DE BOURGH
AND HER DAUGHTER

1424
01:13:01,000 --> 01:13:05,000
TO WHOM I HAVE
RELATED THE AFFAIR IN FULL.

1425
01:13:05,000 --> 01:13:07,000
THEY AGREE WITH ME
IN APPREHENDING

1426
01:13:07,000 --> 01:13:10,000
THAT THIS FALSE STEP
IN ONE SISTER

1427
01:13:10,000 --> 01:13:12,000
MUST BE INJURIOUS
TO THE FORTUNES

1428
01:13:12,000 --> 01:13:14,000
OF ALL THE OTHERS.

1429
01:13:14,000 --> 01:13:17,000
FOR WHO--
AS LADY CATHERINE HERSELF

1430
01:13:17,000 --> 01:13:19,000
CONDESCENDINGLY SAYS--

1431
01:13:19,000 --> 01:13:24,000
WILL CONNECT THEMSELVES
WITH SUCH A FAMILY?

1432
01:13:28,000 --> 01:13:32,000
WHO INDEED, SIR?

1433
01:13:32,000 --> 01:13:35,000
NOW, PERHAPS,
IN VIEW OF THAT CONSIDERATION

1434
01:13:35,000 --> 01:13:38,000
YOU MAY FEEL THAT
IT WOULD BE UNWISE

1435
01:13:38,000 --> 01:13:39,000
FOR YOU TO STAY

1436
01:13:39,000 --> 01:13:42,000
ANY LONGER NOW.

1437
01:13:42,000 --> 01:13:44,000
WELL... WELL,
PERHAPS YOU ARE RIGHT.

1438
01:13:44,000 --> 01:13:47,000
YES, PERHAPS YOU ARE RIGHT,
COUSIN ELIZABETH.

1439
01:13:47,000 --> 01:13:49,000
I ALWAYS FEEL
THAT A CLERGYMAN

1440
01:13:49,000 --> 01:13:52,000
CANNOT BE TOO CAREFUL.

1441
01:13:52,000 --> 01:13:54,000
ESPECIALLY ONE
SO FORTUNATE

1442
01:13:54,000 --> 01:13:55,000
AS TO ENJOY
THE CONDESCENSION

1443
01:13:55,000 --> 01:13:58,000
AND THE PATRONAGE
OF LADY CATHERINE DE BOURGH.

1444
01:13:58,000 --> 01:14:01,000
YOUR THOUGHTFULNESS
DOES YOU CREDIT

1445
01:14:01,000 --> 01:14:06,000
COUSIN ELIZABETH.

1446
01:14:07,000 --> 01:14:09,000
I AM VERY

1447
01:14:09,000 --> 01:14:14,000
VERY SORRY FOR YOU ALL.

1448
01:14:25,000 --> 01:14:26,000
INSUFFERABLE MAN.

1449
01:14:26,000 --> 01:14:28,000
I SUPPOSE
HE MEANS WELL.

1450
01:14:28,000 --> 01:14:30,000
YOU SUPPOSE WRONGLY, JANE.

1451
01:14:30,000 --> 01:14:33,000
HIS PURPOSE IN COMING
WAS TO ENJOY OUR MISFORTUNES

1452
01:14:33,000 --> 01:14:36,000
AND CONGRATULATE HIMSELF
ON HIS OWN HAPPY SITUATION.

1453
01:14:36,000 --> 01:14:38,000
Mary:
I THINK IT VERY KIND OF HIM

1454
01:14:38,000 --> 01:14:43,000
TO VISIT
AND CONDOLE WITH US.

1455
01:14:44,000 --> 01:14:45,000
IS HE GONE?

1456
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:48,000
YES.

1457
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:49,000
GOOD.

1458
01:14:49,000 --> 01:14:51,000
Lizzy:
FOREVER, WITH ANY LUCK.

1459
01:14:51,000 --> 01:14:52,000
Kitty:
HERE'S AUNT PHILLIPS!

1460
01:14:52,000 --> 01:14:54,000
SHE CAN TELL US
THE NEWS FROM MERYTON.

1461
01:14:54,000 --> 01:14:57,000
I DOUBT THERE'S MUCH
WE'D CARE TO HEAR.

1462
01:14:57,000 --> 01:14:58,000
OUR MOTHER
WILL BE PLEASED

1463
01:14:58,000 --> 01:15:00,000
TO SEE HER.

1464
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:02,000
WELL, GIRLS, HERE'S A TO-DO.

1465
01:15:02,000 --> 01:15:05,000
DOES YOUR MOTHER
STILL KEEP TO HER BED?

1466
01:15:05,000 --> 01:15:07,000
SHE IS NOT IN BED,
BUT SHE KEEPS

1467
01:15:07,000 --> 01:15:08,000
TO HER ROOM.

1468
01:15:08,000 --> 01:15:12,000
WELL, THE LESS THE SERVANTS
HEAR, THE BETTER, I DARESAY.

1469
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:14,000
COME, LET ME
TO HER, JANE

1470
01:15:14,000 --> 01:15:19,000
THOUGH HEAVEN KNOWS
I'VE NO GLAD TIDINGS
FOR HER.

1471
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:23,000
NOT A DAY GOES BY BUT I HEAR
SOME BAD TALE OF MR. WICKHAM.

1472
01:15:23,000 --> 01:15:25,000
OH, MR. WICKHAM--

1473
01:15:25,000 --> 01:15:27,000
THAT EVERYBODY
PRAISED TO THE SKIES.

1474
01:15:27,000 --> 01:15:28,000
MR. WICKHAM

1475
01:15:28,000 --> 01:15:31,000
THAT HALF THE TOWN
WAS MAD IN LOVE WITH--

1476
01:15:31,000 --> 01:15:33,000
ALL THE TIME A VILLAIN

1477
01:15:33,000 --> 01:15:37,000
A VERY DEMON FROM HELL
SENT TO RUIN US.

1478
01:15:37,000 --> 01:15:39,000
I HAVE HEARD HE'S RUN UP DEBTS

1479
01:15:39,000 --> 01:15:42,000
WITH EVERY REPUTABLE TRADESMAN
IN THE TOWN.

1480
01:15:42,000 --> 01:15:44,000
OH, SISTER.

1481
01:15:44,000 --> 01:15:46,000
I HAVE HEARD TALES
OF GAMING DEBTS...

1482
01:15:46,000 --> 01:15:47,000
OH, SISTER.

1483
01:15:47,000 --> 01:15:48,000
OF DRUNKEN ROUTS

1484
01:15:48,000 --> 01:15:51,000
IN WHICH MORE THINGS
WERE BROKEN BEYOND REPAIR

1485
01:15:51,000 --> 01:15:53,000
THAN HEADS
AND FURNITURE, SISTER.

1486
01:15:53,000 --> 01:15:55,000
OH, SISTER, STOP.

1487
01:15:55,000 --> 01:15:57,000
DEBAUCHES,
INTRIGUES, SEDUCTIONS.

1488
01:15:57,000 --> 01:15:59,000
THEY SAY THERE'S HARDLY

1489
01:15:59,000 --> 01:16:00,000
A TRADESMAN IN THE TOWN

1490
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:02,000
WHOSE DAUGHTERS
WERE NOT MEDDLED WITH.

1491
01:16:02,000 --> 01:16:05,000
OH! AND NOW HE'S MEDDLING
WITH OUR DEAREST GIRL.

1492
01:16:05,000 --> 01:16:07,000
THE FOUL FIEND!

1493
01:16:07,000 --> 01:16:09,000
WELL, HE SHALL
BE DISCOVERED

1494
01:16:09,000 --> 01:16:12,000
AND MADE TO MARRY HER.

1495
01:16:12,000 --> 01:16:17,000
I HAVE TO SAY, SISTER,
THAT I ALWAYS DISTRUSTED

1496
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:18,000
HIS APPEARANCE
OF GOODNESS.

1497
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:22,000
AYE, SISTER, SO DID I,
AND WARNED THE GIRLS.

1498
01:16:22,000 --> 01:16:25,000
TOO SMOOTH
AND PLAUSIBLE BY HALF.

1499
01:16:25,000 --> 01:16:27,000
BUT WOULD ANYBODY
LISTEN TO ME?

1500
01:16:27,000 --> 01:16:30,000
AND NOW WE ARE ALL,
ALL RUINED.

1501
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:32,000
OH, MY POOR GIRL.

1502
01:16:32,000 --> 01:16:35,000
MY POOR, POOR LYDIA.

1503
01:16:35,000 --> 01:16:40,000
( humming )

1504
01:16:43,000 --> 01:16:45,000
WHEN SHALL WE TRAVEL

1505
01:16:45,000 --> 01:16:47,000
INTO HERTFORDSHIRE,
MY LOVE?

1506
01:16:47,000 --> 01:16:49,000
COME AWAY
FROM THE WINDOW, DEAR.

1507
01:16:49,000 --> 01:16:51,000
WHEN I'VE SETTLED
MY BUSINESS AFFAIRS.

1508
01:16:51,000 --> 01:16:53,000
THESE THINGS
ALWAYS TAKE LONGER

1509
01:16:53,000 --> 01:16:55,000
THAN ONE THINKS THEY WILL.

1510
01:16:55,000 --> 01:16:57,000
YOU'RE NOT UNHAPPY, SURELY?

1511
01:16:57,000 --> 01:16:59,000
LORD, NO.

1512
01:16:59,000 --> 01:17:02,000
JUST THAT I CAN'T WAIT
TO SEE MY MOTHER'S FACE.

1513
01:17:02,000 --> 01:17:04,000
AND MY SISTERS.

1514
01:17:04,000 --> 01:17:05,000
KITTY WILL BE SO ENVIOUS.

1515
01:17:05,000 --> 01:17:07,000
HOW I SHALL LAUGH.

1516
01:17:07,000 --> 01:17:10,000
I HOPE WE SHALL BE MARRIED
FROM LONGBOURN.

1517
01:17:10,000 --> 01:17:11,000
THEN ALL MY SISTERS

1518
01:17:11,000 --> 01:17:14,000
WILL HAVE TO BE
MY BRIDESMAIDS.

1519
01:17:14,000 --> 01:17:18,000
OH, I DO WISH
WE COULD GO OUT INTO THE TOWN

1520
01:17:18,000 --> 01:17:20,000
AND BE SEEN AT PLAYS
AND ASSEMBLIES.

1521
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:22,000
ALL IN GOOD TIME.

1522
01:17:22,000 --> 01:17:26,000
BE PATIENT, DEAR.

1523
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:29,000
LORD, IT MAKES ME WANT
TO BURST OUT LAUGHING

1524
01:17:29,000 --> 01:17:31,000
WHEN I THINK
THAT I HAVE DONE

1525
01:17:31,000 --> 01:17:33,000
WHAT NONE
OF MY SISTERS HAS.

1526
01:17:33,000 --> 01:17:38,000
AND I THE YOUNGEST
OF THEM ALL.

1527
01:17:41,000 --> 01:17:42,000
MOTHER!

1528
01:17:42,000 --> 01:17:46,000
HERE IS A LETTER
FROM MY UNCLE GARDINER!

1529
01:17:46,000 --> 01:17:48,000
FATHER IS COMING HOME TODAY.

1530
01:17:48,000 --> 01:17:50,000
AND DOES HE BRING LYDIA?

1531
01:17:50,000 --> 01:17:51,000
NO.

1532
01:17:51,000 --> 01:17:54,000
THEY HAVE NOT YET
DISCOVERED WHERE SHE IS.

1533
01:17:54,000 --> 01:17:57,000
MY UNCLE WILL CONTINUE
HIS ENQUIRIES ALONE.

1534
01:17:57,000 --> 01:17:58,000
COMING HOME WITHOUT POOR LYDIA?

1535
01:17:58,000 --> 01:18:01,000
WHO WILL FIGHT WICKHAM
AND MAKE HIM MARRY HER

1536
01:18:01,000 --> 01:18:02,000
IF HE COMES AWAY?

1537
01:18:02,000 --> 01:18:06,000
OH, JANE, JANE,
WHAT IS TO BECOME OF US?

1538
01:18:06,000 --> 01:18:09,000
OH! OH, FETCH MY SMELLING SALTS.

1539
01:18:09,000 --> 01:18:12,000
I FEEL MY FAINTNESS
COMING UPON ME AGAIN.

1540
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:13,000
OH!

1541
01:18:13,000 --> 01:18:15,000
OH!

1542
01:18:15,000 --> 01:18:17,000
OH!

1543
01:18:17,000 --> 01:18:22,000
( cries out )

1544
01:18:22,000 --> 01:18:24,000
NOT NOW, JANE.

1545
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:29,000
NOT NOW, LIZZY.

1546
01:19:18,000 --> 01:19:23,000
( gasps )

1547
01:19:24,000 --> 01:19:29,000
MRS. YOUNGE...

1548
01:19:31,000 --> 01:19:32,000
SHOULD I GO
AND GET FATHER?

1549
01:19:32,000 --> 01:19:34,000
HE HAS HAD
NOTHING TO EAT

1550
01:19:34,000 --> 01:19:36,000
SINCE HE CAME HOME.

1551
01:19:36,000 --> 01:19:37,000
LET ME.

1552
01:19:37,000 --> 01:19:42,000
YOU TAKE MOTHER
HER TEA.

1553
01:19:42,000 --> 01:19:47,000
( door opens )

1554
01:19:57,000 --> 01:19:59,000
WELL, JANE.

1555
01:19:59,000 --> 01:20:01,000
ELIZABETH.

1556
01:20:01,000 --> 01:20:05,000
MARY. KITTY.

1557
01:20:05,000 --> 01:20:08,000
YOU LOOK SO TIRED, FATHER.

1558
01:20:08,000 --> 01:20:11,000
IT MUST HAVE BEEN
A DREADFUL TIME FOR YOU.

1559
01:20:11,000 --> 01:20:12,000
SAY NOTHING OF THAT.

1560
01:20:12,000 --> 01:20:15,000
WHO SHOULD SUFFER BUT MYSELF?

1561
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:17,000
IT HAS BEEN
MY OWN DOING

1562
01:20:17,000 --> 01:20:19,000
AND I OUGHT
TO FEEL IT.

1563
01:20:19,000 --> 01:20:20,000
OH, PAPA.

1564
01:20:20,000 --> 01:20:23,000
YOU MUST NOT
BE SO SEVERE

1565
01:20:23,000 --> 01:20:24,000
UPON YOURSELF.

1566
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:25,000
NO, LIZZY, LET ME

1567
01:20:25,000 --> 01:20:28,000
FOR ONCE IN MY LIFE FEEL
HOW MUCH I HAVE BEEN TO BLAME.

1568
01:20:28,000 --> 01:20:31,000
I AM NOT AFRAID
OF BEING OVERPOWERED
BY THE IMPRESSION.

1569
01:20:31,000 --> 01:20:35,000
IT WILL PASS AWAY SOON ENOUGH.

1570
01:20:35,000 --> 01:20:39,000
DO YOU STILL SUPPOSE THEM
TO BE IN LONDON, SIR?

1571
01:20:39,000 --> 01:20:43,000
YES. WHERE ELSE
CAN THEY BE SO WELL CONCEALED?

1572
01:20:43,000 --> 01:20:46,000
AND LYDIA ALWAYS WANTED
TO GO TO LONDON.

1573
01:20:46,000 --> 01:20:48,000
SHE IS HAPPY, THEN

1574
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:53,000
AND HER RESIDENCE THERE WILL
PROBABLY BE OF SOME DURATION.

1575
01:20:55,000 --> 01:20:58,000
LIZZY, I BEAR YOU
NO ILL WILL

1576
01:20:58,000 --> 01:21:02,000
FOR BEING JUSTIFIED
IN YOUR ADVICE TO ME IN MAY

1577
01:21:02,000 --> 01:21:04,000
WHICH, CONSIDERING THE EVENT

1578
01:21:04,000 --> 01:21:08,000
SHOWS SOME GREATNESS
OF MIND, I THINK.

1579
01:21:08,000 --> 01:21:09,000
I MUST

1580
01:21:09,000 --> 01:21:12,000
TAKE MAMMA HER TEA.

1581
01:21:12,000 --> 01:21:16,000
SHE STILL KEEPS HER STATE
ABOVESTAIRS, DOES SHE?

1582
01:21:16,000 --> 01:21:19,000
GOOD. IT LENDS SUCH AN ELEGANCE
TO OUR MISFORTUNE.

1583
01:21:19,000 --> 01:21:21,000
ANOTHER TIME I'LL DO THE SAME.

1584
01:21:21,000 --> 01:21:23,000
I'LL SIT IN MY LIBRARY

1585
01:21:23,000 --> 01:21:25,000
IN MY NIGHTCAP
AND POWDERING GOWN

1586
01:21:25,000 --> 01:21:28,000
AND I'LL GIVE
AS MUCH TROUBLE
AS I CAN.

1587
01:21:28,000 --> 01:21:32,000
PERHAPS I MAY DEFER IT
TILL KITTY RUNS AWAY.

1588
01:21:32,000 --> 01:21:34,000
I'M NOT GOING
TO RUN AWAY, PAPA.

1589
01:21:34,000 --> 01:21:37,000
IF I SHOULD GO TO BRIGHTON

1590
01:21:37,000 --> 01:21:38,000
I WOULD BEHAVE
BETTER THAN LYDIA.

1591
01:21:38,000 --> 01:21:39,000
YOU GO TO BRIGHTON?

1592
01:21:39,000 --> 01:21:42,000
I WOULDN'T TRUST YOU
AS NEAR IT AS EASTBOURNE.

1593
01:21:42,000 --> 01:21:43,000
NOT FOR £50.

1594
01:21:43,000 --> 01:21:44,000
NO, KITTY

1595
01:21:44,000 --> 01:21:47,000
I HAVE AT LAST
LEARNED TO BE CAUTIOUS.

1596
01:21:47,000 --> 01:21:49,000
YOU WILL FEEL
THE EFFECTS OF IT.

1597
01:21:49,000 --> 01:21:52,000
NO OFFICER IS EVER
TO ENTER MY HOUSE AGAIN.

1598
01:21:52,000 --> 01:21:54,000
OR EVEN TO PASS
THROUGH THE VILLAGE.

1599
01:21:54,000 --> 01:21:58,000
BALLS WILL BE
ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED

1600
01:21:58,000 --> 01:22:01,000
UNLESS YOU STAND UP
WITH ONE OF YOUR SISTERS.

1601
01:22:01,000 --> 01:22:03,000
AND YOU ARE NEVER TO STIR

1602
01:22:03,000 --> 01:22:04,000
OUT OF DOORS

1603
01:22:04,000 --> 01:22:07,000
UNTIL YOU CAN PROVE
YOU'VE SPENT TEN MINUTES

1604
01:22:07,000 --> 01:22:09,000
OF EVERY DAY
IN A RATIONAL MANNER.

1605
01:22:09,000 --> 01:22:12,000
WELL, WELL, DON'T MAKE
YOURSELF UNHAPPY, MY DEAR.

1606
01:22:12,000 --> 01:22:14,000
IF YOU'RE A GOOD GIRL

1607
01:22:14,000 --> 01:22:16,000
FOR THE NEXT TEN YEARS

1608
01:22:16,000 --> 01:22:19,000
I'LL TAKE YOU TO A REVUE
AT THE END OF THEM.

1609
01:22:19,000 --> 01:22:24,000
( sobbing )

1610
01:22:47,000 --> 01:22:51,000
OH, DEAREST,
SHALL WE NOT GO OUT TONIGHT?

1611
01:22:51,000 --> 01:22:55,000
CAN WE NOT GO
TO THE THEATER?

1612
01:22:55,000 --> 01:22:58,000
LORD! WHAT IN THE WORLD
IS HE DOING HERE?

1613
01:22:58,000 --> 01:23:00,000
WHAT?

1614
01:23:00,000 --> 01:23:01,000
WHAT A JOKE.

1615
01:23:01,000 --> 01:23:03,000
WHO? WHO IS IT?

1616
01:23:03,000 --> 01:23:04,000
YOU WILL NEVER GUESS.

1617
01:23:04,000 --> 01:23:06,000
WHO IS IT?!

1618
01:23:06,000 --> 01:23:11,000
MR. DARCY.

1619
01:23:37,000 --> 01:23:42,000
COME IN.

1620
01:23:44,000 --> 01:23:49,000
THANK YOU, HILL.

1621
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:02,000
YES, HILL, WHAT IS IT?

1622
01:24:02,000 --> 01:24:04,000
IS MRS. BENNET
ASKING FOR ONE OF US?

1623
01:24:04,000 --> 01:24:06,000
NO, MA'AM.

1624
01:24:06,000 --> 01:24:08,000
I BEG YOUR PARDON,
BUT DID YOU KNOW

1625
01:24:08,000 --> 01:24:10,000
AN EXPRESS COME
FOR MASTER

1626
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:11,000
FROM MR. GARDINER?

1627
01:24:11,000 --> 01:24:13,000
WHEN DID IT COME?

1628
01:24:13,000 --> 01:24:18,000
ABOUT HALF
AN HOUR AGO, MA'AM.

1629
01:24:39,000 --> 01:24:40,000
WELL, LIZZY.

1630
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:43,000
PAPA... WHAT NEWS?

1631
01:24:43,000 --> 01:24:46,000
WHAT NEWS HAVE YOU
HEARD FROM MY UNCLE?

1632
01:24:46,000 --> 01:24:49,000
YES, YES, I'VE HAD
A LETTER FROM HIM.

1633
01:24:49,000 --> 01:24:50,000
WHAT NEWS
DOES IT BRING--

1634
01:24:50,000 --> 01:24:52,000
GOOD OR BAD?

1635
01:24:52,000 --> 01:24:54,000
WHAT IS THERE OF GOOD
TO BE EXPECTED?

1636
01:24:54,000 --> 01:24:58,000
PERHAPS YOU WOULD
LIKE TO READ IT YOURSELF.

1637
01:24:58,000 --> 01:25:00,000
READ IT ALOUD, LIZZY.

1638
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:03,000
I HARDLY KNOW WHAT
TO MAKE OF IT MYSELF.

1639
01:25:03,000 --> 01:25:06,000
"MY DEAR BROTHER, AT LAST
I AM ABLE SEND TIDINGS

1640
01:25:06,000 --> 01:25:08,000
"OF MY NIECE
AND MR. WICKHAM.

1641
01:25:08,000 --> 01:25:09,000
I HAVE SEEN THEM BOTH."

1642
01:25:09,000 --> 01:25:11,000
IT IS AS I HOPED!
THEY ARE MARRIED!

1643
01:25:11,000 --> 01:25:13,000
"THEY ARE NOT MARRIED

1644
01:25:13,000 --> 01:25:16,000
"NOR CAN I FIND THERE WAS
ANY INTENTION OF BEING SO

1645
01:25:16,000 --> 01:25:18,000
"BUT IF YOU PERFORM
THE ENGAGEMENTS

1646
01:25:18,000 --> 01:25:20,000
"I HAVE VENTURED
TO MAKE ON YOUR SIDE

1647
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:22,000
I HOPE IT WILL NOT BE LONG
BEFORE THEY ARE."

1648
01:25:22,000 --> 01:25:23,000
WHAT ENGAGEMENTS?

1649
01:25:23,000 --> 01:25:24,000
READ ON.

1650
01:25:24,000 --> 01:25:26,000
"ALL THAT IS REQUIRED OF YOU

1651
01:25:26,000 --> 01:25:29,000
"IS TO ASSURE YOUR DAUGHTER
HER EQUAL SHARE

1652
01:25:29,000 --> 01:25:32,000
"OF £5,000 SHE WILL
INHERIT ON YOUR DEATH

1653
01:25:32,000 --> 01:25:33,000
"AND ALSO ALLOW HER

1654
01:25:33,000 --> 01:25:36,000
DURING YOUR LIFE...
£100 PER ANNUM."

1655
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:37,000
SO LITTLE.

1656
01:25:37,000 --> 01:25:40,000
WHAT ABOUT
WICKHAM'S DEBTS?

1657
01:25:40,000 --> 01:25:41,000
READ ON.

1658
01:25:41,000 --> 01:25:44,000
"YOU WILL EASILY COMPREHEND
MR. WICKHAM'S CIRCUMSTANCES

1659
01:25:44,000 --> 01:25:45,000
"ARE NOT SO HOPELESS

1660
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:47,000
AS THEY ARE GENERALLY
BELIEVED TO BE."

1661
01:25:47,000 --> 01:25:48,000
THERE.

1662
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:50,000
READ ON, LIZZY.

1663
01:25:50,000 --> 01:25:53,000
"I AM HAPPY TO SAY THERE
WILL BE SOME LITTLE MONEY

1664
01:25:53,000 --> 01:25:55,000
"EVEN WHEN ALL
HIS DEBTS ARE DISCHARGED

1665
01:25:55,000 --> 01:25:57,000
TO SETTLE ON MY NIECE."

1666
01:25:57,000 --> 01:25:59,000
I CANNOT BELIEVE IT.

1667
01:25:59,000 --> 01:26:01,000
READ ON.

1668
01:26:01,000 --> 01:26:03,000
"WE HAVE JUDGED IT BEST

1669
01:26:03,000 --> 01:26:06,000
"THAT MY NIECE SHOULD
BE MARRIED FROM THIS HOUSE.

1670
01:26:06,000 --> 01:26:07,000
I HOPE YOU WILL APPROVE."

1671
01:26:07,000 --> 01:26:09,000
POOR KITTY
WILL BE DISAPPOINTED

1672
01:26:09,000 --> 01:26:11,000
NOT TO BE A BRIDESMAID.

1673
01:26:11,000 --> 01:26:12,000
"SEND BACK YOUR ANSWER SOON

1674
01:26:12,000 --> 01:26:14,000
"AND BE SURE
TO WRITE EXPLICITLY

1675
01:26:14,000 --> 01:26:16,000
"AS TO THE FINANCIAL
SETTLEMENT.

1676
01:26:16,000 --> 01:26:18,000
YOURS, ET CETERA."

1677
01:26:18,000 --> 01:26:20,000
HOW CAN IT BE POSSIBLE

1678
01:26:20,000 --> 01:26:22,000
HE WILL MARRY HER
FOR SO LITTLE?

1679
01:26:22,000 --> 01:26:24,000
Jane:
HE MUST NOT BE UNDESERVING
AS WE THOUGHT.

1680
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:27,000
HE MUST TRULY BE IN LOVE
WITH HER, I THINK.

1681
01:26:27,000 --> 01:26:30,000
YOU THINK THAT, JANE,
IF IT GIVES YOU COMFORT.

1682
01:26:30,000 --> 01:26:32,000
HAVE YOU
ANSWERED THE LETTER?

1683
01:26:32,000 --> 01:26:37,000
NO, BUT I MUST, AND SOON.

1684
01:26:38,000 --> 01:26:40,000
AND THEY MUST MARRY.

1685
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:42,000
YET HE IS SUCH A MAN.

1686
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:43,000
YES, YES

1687
01:26:43,000 --> 01:26:45,000
THEY MUST MARRY.

1688
01:26:45,000 --> 01:26:47,000
THERE IS NOTHING ELSE
TO BE DONE.

1689
01:26:47,000 --> 01:26:49,000
BUT THERE ARE TWO THINGS

1690
01:26:49,000 --> 01:26:50,000
I WANT TO KNOW.

1691
01:26:50,000 --> 01:26:52,000
ONE IS HOW MUCH MONEY

1692
01:26:52,000 --> 01:26:54,000
YOUR UNCLE LAID DOWN
TO BRING THIS ABOUT

1693
01:26:54,000 --> 01:26:59,000
AND THE OTHER...
HOW AM I EVER TO REPAY HIM?

1694
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:04,000
I WISH I HAD NEVER SPOKEN
A WORD OF THIS WHOLE AFFAIR

1695
01:27:04,000 --> 01:27:06,000
TO MR. DARCY.

1696
01:27:06,000 --> 01:27:08,000
DEAR LIZZY, PLEASE
DO NOT DISTRESS YOURSELF.

1697
01:27:08,000 --> 01:27:11,000
I'M SURE MR. DARCY WILL
RESPECT YOUR CONFIDENCE.

1698
01:27:11,000 --> 01:27:14,000
I'M SURE HE WILL.

1699
01:27:14,000 --> 01:27:16,000
THAT IS NOT
WHAT DISTRESSES ME.

1700
01:27:16,000 --> 01:27:18,000
WHAT THEN?

1701
01:27:18,000 --> 01:27:20,000
I DON'T KNOW.

1702
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:25,000
HOW HE MUST BE CONGRATULATING
HIMSELF ON HIS ESCAPE.

1703
01:27:25,000 --> 01:27:28,000
HOW HE MUST DESPISE ME NOW.

1704
01:27:28,000 --> 01:27:30,000
BUT, LIZZY, YOU NEVER
SOUGHT HIS LOVE

1705
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:32,000
NOR WELCOMED IT
WHEN HE OFFERED IT.

1706
01:27:32,000 --> 01:27:35,000
IF HE HAS WITHDRAWN
HIS HIGH OPINION OF YOU NOW

1707
01:27:35,000 --> 01:27:36,000
WHY SHOULD YOU CARE?

1708
01:27:36,000 --> 01:27:39,000
I DON'T KNOW.

1709
01:27:39,000 --> 01:27:43,000
I CAN'T EXPLAIN IT.

1710
01:27:43,000 --> 01:27:48,000
I KNOW I SHALL
PROBABLY NEVER SEE HIM AGAIN.

1711
01:27:48,000 --> 01:27:50,000
I CANNOT BEAR TO THINK

1712
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:53,000
THAT HE IS ALIVE IN THE WORLD

1713
01:27:53,000 --> 01:27:58,000
AND THINKING ILL OF ME.

1714
01:28:07,000 --> 01:28:08,000
( Mrs. Bennet laughing )
OH, I KNEW IT WOULD ALL
COME OUT RIGHT IN THE END.
OH, MY DEAR, DEAR LYDIA.
SHE WILL BE MARRIED.
OH, MY GOOD,
KIND BROTHER.
I KNEW HOW
IT WOULD BE.
I KNEW HE WOULD
MANAGE EVERYTHING.
OH, BUT THE CLOTHES.
SHE MUST BE MARRIED
FROM LONGBOURN.
THIS IS ALL NONSENSE
ABOUT HER BEING MARRIED
FROM CHEAPSIDE.
SHE MUST BE MARRIED
IN LONGBOURN CHURCH
WHERE ALL HER FRIENDS
CAN SEE HER.
THAT IS NOT POSSIBLE.
YOU MUST SEE THAT.
I DO NOT SEE THAT!
WHY SHOULD I SEE THAT?
WHY SHOULD THAT BE?
BECAUSE SHE HAS BEEN LIVING
WITH MR. WICKHAM IN LONDON
AND IF SHE WERE TO ARRIVE
HOME UNMARRIED STILL...
I SUPPOSE IT MUST BE
IF YOU PUT IT LIKE THAT
BUT IT IS ALL VERY VEXING
AND YOUR UNCLE
HAS BEEN MOST HIGH-HANDED.
I DON'T SEE WHY
HE SHOULD TAKE
SO MUCH UPON HIM.
MAMMA, WE ARE GREATLY
INDEBTED TO MR. GARDINER.
HE MUST HAVE LAID OUT
A GREAT DEAL OF MONEY
TO PAY OFF
MR. WICKHAM'S DEBTS--
MORE THAN WE
CAN EVER REPAY.
AND WHY SHOULD HE NOT?
WHO ELSE SHOULD
BUT HER OWN UNCLE?
MOTHER!
OH, WELL, I AM SO HAPPY.
A DAUGHTER MARRIED,
AND ONLY JUST 16!
"MRS. WICKHAM."
OOH, HOW WELL THAT SOUNDS.
OH, BUT THE WEDDING CLOTHES!
LIZZY, MY DEAR
GO DOWN TO YOUR FATHER
AND ASK HOW MUCH
HE WILL GIVE HER.
Mrs. Bennet:
OH, JANE, AS SOON
AS I AM DRESSED
I SHALL GO TO MERYTON
AND TELL MY SISTER PHILLIPS.
RING THE BELL FOR HILL.
AN AIRING WILL DO ME
A GREAT DEAL OF GOOD, I'M SURE
AND I SHALL CALL
ON LADY LUCAS AND MRS. LONG.
OH, JANE!
PAPA.
JANE, IT'S SUCH
WONDERFUL NEWS!
OH, WHERE IS HILL?
OH, HILL, HAVE YOU
HEARD THE GOOD NEWS?
SHUT THE DOOR, LIZZY.
...AND YOU SHALL HAVE
A BOWL OF PUNCH...
SOMEONE, AT LEAST, FINDS
PLEASURE IN THESE EVENTS.
BUT CONSIDERING
WHAT WE THOUGHT
ONLY A FEW HOURS AGO
IT'S NOT SO BAD, IS IT?
DO YOU THINK MY UNCLE
HAD TO PAY OUT
A GREAT DEAL OF MONEY?
I DO. WICKHAM'S A FOOL
IF HE TAKES HER WITH A FARTHING
LESS THAN £10,000.
£10,000!
HEAVEN FORBID.
HOW IS HALF SUCH A SUM
TO BE REPAID?
I WISH I HAD LAID BY
AN ANNUAL SUM
TO BRIBE WORTHLESS YOUNG MEN
TO MARRY MY DAUGHTERS
BUT I HAVE NOT, I CONFESS.
THE REASON WAS, OF COURSE,
I INTENDED TO FATHER A SON.
THE SON WOULD INHERIT THE ESTATE
NO PART OF WHICH
WOULD BE ENTAILED AWAY
SO PROVIDING FOR MY WIDOW
AND ANY OTHER CHILDREN.
BY THE TIME
YOUR MOTHER AND I
HAD ABANDONED HOPE
OF PRODUCING AN HEIR
IT SEEMED A LITTLE LATE
TO BEGIN SAVING.
YOU COULD NOT HAVE
FORESEEN THIS, FATHER.
I SHOULD HAVE TAKEN BETTER CARE
OF YOU ALL.
THE SATISFACTION
OF PREVAILING UPON
ONE OF THE MOST
WORTHLESS YOUNG MEN
IN BRITAIN MIGHT
THEN HAVE RESTED
IN ITS PROPER PLACE.
AS IT IS, THE THING IS DONE
WITH EXTRAORDINARY LITTLE
INCONVENIENCE TO MYSELF.
WHEN YOU TAKE INTO ACCOUNT
WHAT I SHALL SAVE
ON LYDIA'S BOARD
AND POCKET ALLOWANCE
I'M SCARCELY TEN POUNDS
A YEAR WORSE OFF.
I'M HEARTILY ASHAMED
OF MYSELF, LIZZY.
BUT DON'T DESPAIR...
IT WILL PASS...
AND NO DOUBT MORE QUICKLY
THAN IT SHOULD.
WHERE IS EVERYONE?
DEARLY BELOVED
WE ARE GATHERED HERE
IN THE SIGHT OF GOD...
Gardiner:
"MR. WICKHAM IS TO RESIGN
FROM THE MILITIA
"AND GO
INTO A NORTHERN REGIMENT.
"HAPPILY, THERE ARE STILL SOME
AMONG HIS FORMER FRIENDS
"WHO ARE WILLING TO ASSIST HIM
"IN PURCHASING A COMMISSION.
"I HAVE WRITTEN
TO COLONEL FORSTER
"TO REQUEST THAT HE WILL SATISFY
"MR. WICKHAM'S CREDITORS
IN BRIGHTON
FOR WHICH
I HAVE PLEDGED MYSELF."
"PERHAPS YOU WILL BE SO GOOD
AS TO DO THE SAME
"FOR HIS CREDITORS IN MERYTON,
OF WHOM I ENCLOSE A LIST
"ACCORDING TO
HIS INFORMATION.
I HOPE AT LEAST HE
HAS NOT DECEIVED US."
LET US ALL HOPE SO.
"AS SOON AS THEY ARE MARRIED,
THEY WILL JOURNEY DIRECTLY
"TO JOIN HIS REGIMENT
IN NEWCASTLE
UNLESS THEY ARE FIRST
INVITED TO LONGBOURN."
OH, YES, MY DEAR MR. BENNET,
OF COURSE THEY MUST COME HERE.
I LONG TO SEE MY DEAR LYDIA
AND DEAR WICKHAM,
TOO, OF COURSE.
BUT IT IS SHOCKING
THAT POOR LYDIA
SHOULD HAVE BEEN SENT AWAY
FROM BRIGHTON--
AND SUCH A FAVORITE
AMONG ALL THE OFFICERS.
THERE WERE SEVERAL
OF THE YOUNG MEN THERE
THAT SHE LIKED VERY MUCH
AND THEY
WILL MISS HER
AS MUCH AS SHE
WILL MISS THEM.
THESE NORTHERN
OFFICERS
MAY NOT BE QUITE
SO PLEASANT.
I'M SURE
OUR YOUNGEST DAUGHTER
WILL HAVE NO DIFFICULTY
IN FINDING FRIENDS
AS SILLY AS SHE IS
IN NEWCASTLE.
SHE HAS A TALENT
FOR MAKING
A SPECTACLE
OF HERSELF.
BUT IF THEY ARE
TO LEAVE BRIGHTON
THEY SHOULD COME
TO HERTFORDSHIRE
AND RESIDE
IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD.
HAYE PARK MIGHT DO
IF THE GOLDINGS
WOULD QUIT IT.
OR THE GREAT HOUSE
AT STOKE
IF THE DRAWING ROOMS
WERE LARGER.
OR PURVIS LODGE.
OH, NO, DEAR,
NOT PURVIS LODGE.
THE ATTICS THERE
ARE DREADFUL.
MRS. BENNET,
BEFORE YOU TAKE ANY
OR ALL OF THESE HOUSES
LET US COME
TO A RIGHT UNDERSTANDING.
INTO ONE HOUSE
IN THE NEIGHBORHOOD
THEY SHALL NEVER
HAVE ADMITTANCE:
Bennet:
MR. AND MRS. WICKHAM WILL NEVER
BE WELCOME TO LONGBOURN.
LORD! IT
SEEMS AN AGE
SINCE WE WERE
AT LONGBOURN.
AND HERE YOU ALL ARE,
JUST THE SAME.
OH, MY DEAR, DEAR LYDIA
AT LAST!
OH, I DO BELIEVE
YOU'VE GROWN.
OH, HOW WE'VE MISSED YOU.
OH, WE'VE BEEN FAR TOO MERRY
TO MISS ANY OF YOU.
WELL, HERE WE ARE.
HAVEN'T I CAUGHT MYSELF
A HANDSOME HUSBAND?
Mrs. Bennet:
INDEED YOU HAVE, MY LOVE.
YOU ARE
VERY WELCOME, SIR.
YOU ARE ALL GOODNESS
AND KINDNESS, MA'AM, AS ALWAYS.
OH, LET ME GIVE YOU
A KISS, THEN.
( giggling )
WELL, SHALL WE GO IN?
OH.
NO, JANE.
I TAKE YOUR PLACE NOW.
YOU MUST GO LOWER,
BECAUSE I AM A MARRIED WOMAN.
"MRS. WICKHAM."
LORD! HOW DROLL THAT SOUNDS.
HOW DO YOU LIKE
MY HUSBAND, LIZZY?
I BELIEVE YOU ENVY ME.
WAS HE NOT A FAVORITE
